{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ChJzLx6y7tvT9GX7c2nL1N","type":"tool_result","content":"979\t2026-10-10 note). The root's `code` slot is plain `{A canonical-vector}`\n980\tof `\"v4\"` vectors, verified to hash to their key and to pass\n981\t`code/well-formed?`. **No native image travels**: a stack or register\n982\treceiver derives `H(A)`/`R(A)` with `derive/stack-image`/`register-image`.\n983\t`requires` carries UCF §7.6.1's map **plus** `:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}`,\n984\tone entry per address in `:yin.k/segments`; the **complete association\n985\trule** is phase-5's: an absent entry **or an empty set** is incomplete\n986\t(`:yin.k/missing :yin.k/trees`, discovery `:incomplete`), and a claimed\n987\taddress alone does not establish retrievability (a known address whose\n988\tread fails now is the medium's `:absent`, not a missing association).\n989\t\n990\t### 6.2 Rows, not datoms\n991\t\n992\t**DECIDED** (ruling 4). No vector is projected to datoms; the direct\n993\tload path is the only path (§10.4).\n994\t\n995\t### 6.3 The free environment: carrier, source, ownership\n996\t\n997\t**DECIDED** by the review's finding and §4.4. The task's initial free\n998\tenvironment travels **once, explicitly**, as the root's `free-env`\n999\tslot, a `:bindings` row (`[S V …]` sorted). Every `E` in the task is a\n1000\tcomplete map and is checked by rules X1 and E2. On lower, the\n1001\tsemantic-register kernel receives it as the machine's base `:env`\n1002\t(`create-vm`'s `:env` option, `semantic_register.cljc:261`); a de Bruijn\n1003\tkernel receives it as its `:free-env` (`stack.cljc:418`) and\n1004\treconstructs positional frames from each `E` by the chain (§4.4).\n1005\t\n1006\t**Where the lift gets it (PROPOSED, the gap the review named).** It is\n1007\t**never recovered from a current `E`** (§4.4). Its source is, per\n1008\tkernel:\n1009\t\n1010\t- **de Bruijn kernels**: the kernel's own `:free-env` field, \"fixed for\n1011\t  this instance\" (`stack.cljc:82`; `register.cljc:50`), read directly.\n1012\t- **the semantic-register kernel**: the evaluator keeps only the\n1013\t  mutable-current `:env` (`RegisterVM` field `env`, \"persistent lexical\n1014\t  scope map\", `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:23`; the old semantic\n1015\t  VM likewise captures the initial env only transiently in `eval`,\n1016\t  `semantic.cljc:874-876`), so no field holds the initial map. The\n1017\t  **composition owns it**: it is the value the composition passed as\n1018\t  `create-vm`'s `:env` (`vm/check-bindings!` of it, `:261`). The lift's\n1019\t  input contract therefore takes it explicitly,\n1020\t  `(rows/lift-task vm serve! {:free-env E₀})`, and refuses\n1021\t  `:yin.k/non-portable :missing-free-env` when the caller supplies none;\n1022\t  the holder and REPL paths that call the lift pass the environment they\n1023\t  constructed the task with. **Coordinated retention seam, recommended**:\n1024\t  4b (stage 3, its track's file) adds an immutable `free-env` field set\n1025\t  once in `create-vm` from the checked `:env` and never written by any\n1026\t  transition, with `gc-roots` listing it; once it lands the lift reads\n1027\t  it when `:free-env` is not supplied and the explicit argument stays as\n1028\t  the override for compositions that constructed the task elsewhere.\n1029\t  Phase 6 does **not** edit `semantic_register.cljc`; 6b depends on the\n1030\t  explicit argument and names the seam as a follow-up (§8.2).\n1031\t\n1032\tMerkle sharing means every `E` whose bindings equal another's shares one\n1033\t`:bindings` row; the root slot is one more reference to a row that\n1034\tusually already exists.\n1035\t\n1036\t---\n1037\t\n1038\t## 7. Lift and lower\n1039\t\n1040\t### 7.1 Lift\n1041\t\n1042\t**DECIDED** (draft §9, UCF §7.8): refuse unless quiescent; refuse the\n1043\tholds (`unliftable-hold`, `handoff.cljc:588`) as `:yin.k/non-portable\n1044\t:reason-mismatch`; classify kind; run the **dependency closure over the\n1045\t`\"v4\"` vectors**, which needs the phase-5 scanners\n1046\t(`scan/requirements`, `scan/free-names`, `scan/free-occurrences` over the\n1047\t§2.3 table: the current `completion/code-facts` reads stack-table\n1048\tpositions and cannot be used), and refuse `:yin.k/unsatisfied` unless\n1049\t`:complete`, `:yin.k/trees` included; number cursor cells (draft §6); walk\n1050\twaits, parked records, the store slice, module stores, the free\n1051\tenvironment (from the kernel's `:free-env` field or the lift's explicit\n1052\t`:free-env` argument, §6.3, never from a current `E`), the result,\n1053\tinstall children; run `frame/defect` over every\n1054\tframe; emit rows and the census. A de Bruijn source walks the frames\n1055\t`layout/lift-act`/`lift-tail` reconstruct.\n1056\t\n1057\t### 7.2 Lower\n1058\t\n1059\t**DECIDED** (draft §8 in order; §3.3): gate, structure, graph, hashes,\n1060\tcanonical form, canonical numbering, **frames**, pending and operations,\n1061\tdependency closure (`requires`/`code` agree with the census;\n1062\t`:yin.k/trees` complete per §6.1), custody, composition, restore. Restore\n1063\tbuilds the receiving kernel's state: semantic-register: `code` through\n1064\t`load-vector`/`attach-image` under `code/contract`, the free environment\n1065\tas base `:env`, each `:wait` to an engine entry (payload plus the\n1066\tpending's engine fields, `lower-frame!`'s shapes, `handoff.cljc:3182-3246`,\n1067\t`:deliver` carried), parked records into `:parked`, the result into\n1068\t`:value`; de Bruijn: derive and attach the image for each A, set\n1069\t`:free-env`, and `layout/lower-act`/`lower-tail` each frame (the stack\n1070\tlane's `tail` needs 6c-pre). Restoration delivers nothing, runs nothing,\n1071\tmints nothing.\n1072\t\n1073\t---\n1074\t\n1075\t## 8. Slices, gates, entry conditions\n1076\t\n1077\tVerification follows `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`: G0 per iteration on\n1078\tthe JVM, G1 `bb test:sub yin.vm` on three hosts, G2 `bb test:changed`,\n1079\tG3 on master.\n1080\t\n1081\t### 8.1 Slice 6a: the frame validator and the row codec (independent)\n1082\t\n1083\t**Files to create.**\n1084\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc` (§3): `defect`, public.\n1085\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (§2): the row table as data,\n1086\t  `frame->rows`, `rows->frame`, row ids (Jing default), the census and\n1087\t  numbering per the draft §6, `canonical-under` (§5.5, test-only but\n1088\t  placed here so three test namespaces share it). **Not** `lift-task`/\n1089\t  `lower-task`: full task transport is 6b.\n1090\t- `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc`,\n1091\t  `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc`.\n1092\t\n1093\t**Depends on:** phase 3, 4a (landed), 4b stage 1 (branch) for live\n1094\tframes to validate. Touches nothing of 4b or 5; needs no scanner.\n1095\t\n1096\t**Acceptance (6a).**\n1097\t\n1098\t1. `frame-test/contract-is-pure`: `frame/defect` takes `[frame code\n1099\t   context task]`, `task` being plain data; the namespace's `ns` form\n1100\t   requires no kernel and no `yin.vm.engine` (a string check over the\n1101\t   source on the JVM lane, `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`).\n1102\t2. `frame-test/every-reference-frame-validates`: for every 4b-stage-1\n1103\t   row of §5.2 (1, 2, 5, 6, 13-16, 18, 19, 21, 22) over the four segments,\n1104\t   plus row 20 as one separate, unwrapped run (its empty `K` needs no wrapper\n1105\t   frames; §8.2 6b makes the same exception), every\n1106\t   `act`, `tail`, return frame, parked record and reified value the\n1107\t   register evaluator mints passes `defect` in its context with the\n1108\t   task context decoded from the machine's own tables.\n1109\t3. `frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper`: for each rule S1-S4, C1-C3,\n1110\t   A1-A6, T1, K1-K3, E1-E2, X1, P1-P4 one tampered frame built from a\n1111\t   valid one, refused with that rule's kind and a path naming the slot\n1112\t   (**twenty-four rules**: 4+3+6+1+3+2+1+4, the twenty-three of the\n1113\t   round-1 text plus X1; **twenty-five rows**, since C2 contributes two,\n1114\t   a float `pc` for `:pc-kind` and an out-of-range one for `:pc-bounds`;\n1115\t   X1's row goes through `frame/task-defect`); plus\n1116\t   `first-defect-is-structural`: a frame with a malformed `K` **and** a\n1117\t   bad window reports `:k-shape`.\n1118\t4. `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member`: row 22's frame\n1119\t   validates with the nil key present; the same frame with the key\n1120\t   removed is `:window-missing`.\n1121\t5. `frame-test/worked-example-saved`: on `:worked-example`, a frame at pc\n1122\t   4 with window `{1 <f>}` and `rd 2` validates; `{1 <f> 2 x}` is\n1123\t   `:window-self`; `{}` is `:window-missing`; `{1 <f> 3 x}` is\n1124\t   `:window-extra` (`saved(4, 2) = {1}`, `analysis_test.cljc:131-139`).\n1125\t6. `frame-test/free-env-mismatch`: row 21's frame (initial free\n1126\t   environment `{x 99 y 7}`) with `task :free-env {x 99 y 7}` validates;\n1127\t   with the free environment `{x 99 y 8}` or `{x 99}` it is\n1128\t   `:free-env-mismatch` (`y` is unshadowed); with the lexical `x` removed\n1129\t   from `E` it is `:free-env-mismatch` (presence); changing the lexical\n1130\t   `x` in `E` from `1` to `98` **does not** trip E2 (it is off the\n1131\t   comparison), and the test asserts that too; a `free-env` row with the\n1132\t   key `yin/def` is `:reserved-name` (X1).\n1133\t7. `rows-test/bijection`: `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame` and the converse\n1134\t   are identities on every frame of item 2, nil-valued keys included.\n1135\t8. `rows-test/row-ids-are-jing-default`: every content row's id equals\n1136\t   `(jing/segment-key body)` and names Jing's default algorithm; no\n1137\t   `sha256` appears in any id.\n1138\t9. `rows-test/window-sorted-and-unique`: an out-of-order or duplicated\n1139\t   `:window` row is `:yin.k/undecodable` at canonical form (step 5).\n1140\t10. `rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`: §5.5's\n1141\t    transformation gives equal root ids for two emissions of one abstract\n1142\t    task under permuted cursor-cell numbering and distinct stream identities,\n1143\t    with the fixture's correspondence map; **and the unordered-container\n1144\t    permutation**: a store value that is a set of two stream references\n1145\t    and a map keyed by two cursor references, emitted twice with the two\n1146\t    streams' identities swapped (and the correspondence map swapped\n1147\t    accordingly), gives equal root ids; a marker absent from the map is\n1148\t    a test failure.\n1149\t11. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log\n1150\t    shows `Testing yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test` and\n1151\t    `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`.\n1152\t12. `rows-test/discovery-order-numbering`: `canonical-numbering` returns\n1153\t    the maps of the numbering note's appendix A for `fixture :s1 :s2 :x\n1154\t    :y`, the review counterexample, `[x x y]`, `[x y y]`, `[#{X Y} X]`,\n1155\t    the witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]`, `[#{X Y} #{Y Z}]`, the path and\n1156\t    the two frame fixtures.\n1157\t13. `rows-test/occurrence-count-separates-members`: the review\n1158\t    counterexample numbers `Y cc-1, X cc-2`, pinned `2d9873a8…`; the path\n1159\t    pinned `726a9fbb…`; `[#{X Y} #{Y Z}]` pinned `d84480d4…`; each equal\n1160\t    after renaming plus reversal of every set.\n1161\t14. `rows-test/interchangeable-ties`: `#{X Y}`, `#{[X X] [Y Y]}`,\n1162\t    `{X 1, Y 1}`, `#{#{X Y} #{Z W}}` number without refusal; reversal and\n1163\t    renaming give equal roots; pins `07eda35d…`, `da69c679…`,\n1164\t    `49d4478c…`, `18b70de6…`.\n1165\t15. `rows-test/alias-pattern-is-part-of-the-key`: `#{[X X] [Y Z]}` and\n1166\t    `{X X, Y Z}` give one root for both enumerations and after renaming,\n1167\t    pinned `387f294a…` and `be62ba43…`; the witness numbers `B cc-1,\n1168\t    A cc-2`, pinned `0193312…`, and decodes; the balanced-alias witness\n1169\t    `#{[X X Y Y] [Z W Z W]}` gives one root for both enumerations, pinned\n1170\t    `5376f133…`, and the key without the local index would not.\n1171\t16. `rows-test/unresolved-cursor-cells-refuse`: the 2-cycle, the\n1172\t    3-cycle, the loop plus 2-cycle, the seven-cell state,\n1173\t    `[#{X Y} #{X Y}]`, the mixed-body, the anchored, the two-2-cycle and\n1174\t    the 3-cycle-beside-fan states refuse at `emit` with\n1175\t    `:yin.k/non-portable :unresolved-cursor-cells`, the paths and cells of\n1176\t    the numbering note's appendix A, the same verdict and path after\n1177\t    renaming plus shuffling; a carrier of each built with `emit-numbered`\n1178\t    decodes to `:yin.k/undecodable :unresolved-cursor-cells` with the\n1179\t    path prefixed by the root, never `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`; a\n1180\t    parent whose install `'a` holds the 2-cycle refuses at `emit` with\n1181\t    path `[12 a 15]` and its `emit-numbered` carrier decodes to the\n1182\t    `:yin.k/undecodable` kind with path `[<root> 12 a 15]`.\n1183\t17. `rows-test/canonical-roots-are-pinned`: `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n1184\t    unchanged; `a850fce6…` (`[#{X Y} X]`), `4993b5b1…`, `536c810b…`,\n1185\t    `e67405ec…` (`[#{#{X Y} #{Z W}} X]`), `6e7c7a6b…` (ten cells) added;\n1186\t    `55ff168e…` removed.\n1187\t18. `rows-test/counterexample-search`: a seeded generator (at least 2000\n1188\t    random value states, 200 frame-bearing, 100 with install children)\n1189\t    in CI: every numbered state's carrier decodes and re-emits to its\n1190\t    root; renaming every cursor cell plus shuffling every set, map and\n1191\t    census gives an equal root, or the same refusal verdict and path;\n1192\t    refusals are counted and reported; the largest `:work` is reported.\n1193\t19. `rows-test/numbering-is-total`: a census cell the walk does not reach\n1194\t    raises the totality defect, not a refusal, before any row is emitted.\n1195\t20. `numbering-precedes-frame-defect`, `alias-topology-and-census`,\n1196\t    `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`,\n1197\t    `unordered-containers-are-order-free`,\n1198\t    `child-scope-and-shared-child-dag` and\n1199\t    `census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` pass unchanged against the\n1200\t    rewritten decoder; `numbering-precedes-frame-defect` is extended: the\n1201\t    2-cycle with the same reserved-name binding, carried by\n1202\t    `emit-numbered`, decodes to `:yin.k/undecodable\n1203\t    :unresolved-cursor-cells`, not `:reserved-name`.\n1204\t21. `rows-test/gates-and-work`: 65 cells refuse `:resource-limit\n1205\t    [:cursor-cells]` under the default budget and 2 cells under\n1206\t    `{:cursor-cells 1}`; `[[[[X]]]]` under `{:depth 3}` refuses\n1207\t    `[:depth]`, and so do one cell inside 3000 nested vectors under\n1208\t    `{:depth 3}` and under the default budget, and a literal nested 3000\n1209\t    deep beside a cell (no host stack overflow on any of the three hosts;\n1210\t    200 nested vectors number); a set holding a 400000-scalar literal\n1211\t    refuses `[:work]` under `{:work 2000}` with the work counter at 2001\n1212\t    and under `{:work 900000}` with at most 1000 estimator steps; a state\n1213\t    whose bodies carry a 65536-character descriptor numbers under the\n1214\t    default budget; `{:work 1}` refuses `[:work]` at `emit` and, for a\n1215\t    valid carrier, at `decode`.\n1216\t22. Budgets: `:label-bytes` and `:search` gone, `:work` default\n1217\t    `4194304`.\n1218\t\n1219\t### 8.2 Slice 6b: full task transport and the harness on the reference lane\n1220\t\n1221\t**Files to change.** `rows.cljc`: `lift-task`, `lower-task` (§7), the\n1222\tpending rows' lift and lower, install children. **Files to create.**\n1223\t`test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (§5, the\n1224\t`:semantic-register` lane). The old harness file is not edited.\n1225\t\n1226\t**Depends on:** the explicit `:free-env` lift argument supplied by the\n1227\tharness (§6.3; the 4b retention seam is a named follow-up for the 4b\n1228\ttrack, not a 6b prerequisite); 4b stage 2 (FFI retained→sent restoration, link\n1229\trequest/response/install preservation, install children, the\n1230\tevaluator's `IModuleKernel` linking methods: `link-format`,\n1231\t`spawn-module`, `lift-closure`, `lower-closure`); **phase 5c** (the\n1232\t`scan` namespace, for the dependency closure over `\"v4\"` vectors, §7.1).\n1233\tTouches nothing of 4b or 5.\n1234\t\n1235\t**Acceptance (6b).**\n1236\t\n1237\t1. `every-row-every-segment-matches-the-reference`: rows 1-19, 21, 22\n1238\t   and 24 of §5.2 × four segments, plus row 20 once (outside the\n1239\t   wrappers, §5.2), on the reference lane; laws 1-3 and 6; counts\n1240\t   asserted (22 wrapped rows × 4 segments + 1 = 89 runs).\n1241\t2. `tail-states-carry-no-window`: rows 6, 9, 12, 20 lift to `:tail`\n1242\t   rows of three slots and lower to through-`K` delivery.\n1243\t3. `install-rows-carry-the-child`: rows 10-12; the child's kind and\n1244\t   phase as stated; no initialization on lower.\n1245\t4. `captures`: rows 14-16 round-trip; row 15's invocation after lower\n1246\t   delivers once into the captured `rd` and yields `:done`.\n1247\t5. `free-env-shadowing`: row 21 yields `99` after lower.\n1248\t6. `synthetic-tail-bookkeeping`: row 23's hand-built parked `tail`\n1249\t   under a call id in `:ffi-call-ids` passes `defect` with context\n1250\t   `:parked`; the **same valid record under a key absent from\n1251\t   `:ffi-call-ids`** is `:parked-site` (P4); the record with `site` moved\n1252\t   to a non-tail call is `:site` (T1 runs before P4).\n1253\t7. `refusals`: every refusal row of §5.2 refuses with the named status\n1254\t   and kind before any attachment; `first-defect-order`: a body with a\n1255\t   noncanonical cursor-cell numbering **and** a tampered window reports\n1256\t   `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`.\n1257\t8. `a-response-cursor-shared-by-two-waiters-crosses-as-one-cursor-cell` and\n1258\t   `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`, ported.\n1259\t9. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n1260\t\n1261\t### 8.3 Slice 6c: the layouts, the stack seam, the cross-engine lanes\n1262\t\n1263\t**6c-pre, the stack tail-completion seam.** File to change:\n1264\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc` (§4.3): park-entry builders mark a\n1265\ttail-call park `:resume-mode :return-result`; `stack-restore` delivers\n1266\tsuch an entry by the return transition. Test to create:\n1267\t`test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_tail_completion_test.cljc`: a tail\n1268\teffectful call parked and resumed delivers through `K` (pops the frame,\n1269\ttruncates to its base, pushes the value) and halts with the value when\n1270\t`K` is empty; a tail call in operand position never executes the layout\n1271\tsyntax after it; non-tail parks are unchanged (the old stack tests stay\n1272\tgreen). **Depends on** nothing of 4b or 5.\n1273\t\n1274\t**6c proper.** Files to create: `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc`\n1275\t(§4); `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc`; the two extra\n1276\tlanes added to the 6b harness file. **Depends on:** 5a, 5b (`derive`),\n1277\t6b, 6c-pre.\n1278\t\n1279\t**Acceptance (6c).**\n1280\t\n1281\t1. `layout-test/register-pairing`: for every `P ∈ C`, `phys` is total on\n1282\t   every body's named virtuals; `virt(p, s)` is single-valued at every\n1283\t   reachable boundary pc (§5.6 item 3).\n1284\t2. `layout-test/register-live-is-live-out`: §5.6 item 3's second clause,\n1285\t   tail boundaries `[]`.\n1286\t3. `layout-test/register-rd-from-a`: on `:worked-example`'s register\n1287\t   lane at the inner call's park, the canonical `rd` is `2` while the\n1288\t   kernel's `dest` is `3`; the K frame of a nested non-tail call in\n1289\t   `:depth-3` has its `rd` from A, not its physical `dest`.\n1290\t4. `layout-test/stack-correspondence`: §5.6 item 4.\n1291\t5. `layout-test/stack-layout-is-the-saved-set`: §5.6 item 5 and the\n1292\t   worked cases: `(f (g x) y)` at the inner call → `[1]`; `(f (if c (g)\n1293\t   2) y)` at `(g)` → `[1]`.\n1294\t6. `layout-test/stack-slices-partition`: §5.6 item 9; and the\n1295\t   multi-frame fixture, the expression `(cat [1] ((fn [x] (cat [2] ((fn\n1296\t   [y] (cat [3] (next-of c))) 2))) 1))` under the harness's standard\n1297\t   binding setup: `with-cat` outermost, then `(let1 s (stream/make 4)\n1298\t   (let1 c (cursor-of s) …))` around it (the stream is made inside the\n1299\t   program, as every row does: that is this fixture's chosen setup. A\n1300\t   primitive `cat` supplied in the free environment would sit in a live\n1301\t   slot and is no carrier value, `:continuation-registers`,\n1302\t   `debruijn_register_effects.cljc:196`; an authentic cursor reference is\n1303\t   machine data with an explicit carrier marker, `engine.cljc:899-905`, so\n1304\t   in-program construction of `c` is a fixture choice, not a carrier\n1305\t   restriction). **Derivation of the expression\n1306\t   alone** (`cat` and `c` taken as given): the outer application of\n1307\t   `(fn [x] …)` pops its closure and `1`, leaving the outer `cat` and\n1308\t   `[1]` pushed, so its frame's base is `2`; the inner application leaves\n1309\t   the middle `cat` and `[2]` as well, base `4`; the current activation\n1310\t   has pushed its `cat` and `[3]` and the read has popped its cursor\n1311\t   operand (`stack.cljc:839`), so the operand stack has six values:\n1312\t   slices `[0,2)` = `[cat [1]]`, `[2,4)` = `[cat [2]]`, current `[4,6)` =\n1313\t   `[cat [3]]`, each slice's `stack-layout` being `[operator-rd\n1314\t   literal-rd]` of its `cat` call and equal to that activation's saved\n1315\t   window. **As run**, the three binding applications each pop their\n1316\t   closure and single operand off an otherwise empty stack, so `K` has\n1317\t   **five** frames with bases `0, 0, 0, 2, 4`, slices `[0,0) [0,0) [0,0)\n1318\t   [0,2) [2,4)`, current `[4,6)`, stack length six; the test pins these\n1319\t   bases from the kernel's state, checks the partition, and checks that\n1320\t   lowering the lifted frame emits the same five bases (§4.3; the\n1321\t   before-slice rule would emit `0, 0, 0, 0, 2`).\n1322\t7. `layout-test/env-reconstruction`: §5.6 item 6.\n1323\t8. `layout-test/closures-round-trip`: §5.6 item 7.\n1324\t9. `layout-test/tail-lowering-is-unobservable`: §5.6 item 8.\n1325\t10. `harness/cross-engine-canonical-equality`: law 4 for every row ×\n1326\t    segment under `canonical-under`.\n1327\t11. `harness/cross-engine-lowering`: law 5, six ordered pairs.\n1328\t12. `harness/layout-refusals`: `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` from a kernel\n1329\t    stepped to a non-safepoint pc; a register entry whose `live` was\n1330\t    tampered reconstructs a frame the validator refuses (`:window-extra`\n1331\t    or `:window-missing` by the tamper's direction).\n1332\t13. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n1333\t\n1334\t### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n1335\t\n1336\t**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 7). 6a-6c green on three hosts; the row\n1337\tcarrier the only writer and reader the semantic-register kernel has; a\n1338\tdocumented seam for the holder, checkpoint, ledger and authority paths\n1339\t(phase 7 wires it; phase 6 edits none of them); the Stage D/E scenarios\n1340\t(`stage_e_scenarios.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`) listed with, for\n1341\teach, the §5.2 row that exercises its parking shape; the export-recovery\n1342\tobject (UCF §7.7.4, format version 1 over the old codec) re-based on the\n1343\trow carrier by phase 7, since it embeds a body; and the free-environment\n1344\tretention seam (§6.3) either landed by the 4b track or the explicit\n1345\t`:free-env` argument threaded through the holder's export path.\n1346\t\n1347\t### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n1348\t\n1349\t| | needs | concurrent with |\n1350\t|---|---|---|\n1351\t| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n1352\t| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n1353\t| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n1354\t| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n1355\t\n1356\tNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n1357\t`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\n1358\tregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b921a1a6-65e4-4bc4-853c-fc87c8b912fe","uuid":"d56cb559-eeb8-4b85-bc69-eb55678f7d4f","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:41:54.948Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"2026-10-10 note). The root's `code` slot is plain `{A canonical-vector}`\nof `\"v4\"` vectors, verified to hash to their key and to pass\n`code/well-formed?`. **No native image travels**: a stack or register\nreceiver derives `H(A)`/`R(A)` with `derive/stack-image`/`register-image`.\n`requires` carries UCF §7.6.1's map **plus** `:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}`,\none entry per address in `:yin.k/segments`; the **complete association\nrule** is phase-5's: an absent entry **or an empty set** is incomplete\n(`:yin.k/missing :yin.k/trees`, discovery `:incomplete`), and a claimed\naddress alone does not establish retrievability (a known address whose\nread fails now is the medium's `:absent`, not a missing association).\n\n### 6.2 Rows, not datoms\n\n**DECIDED** (ruling 4). No vector is projected to datoms; the direct\nload path is the only path (§10.4).\n\n### 6.3 The free environment: carrier, source, ownership\n\n**DECIDED** by the review's finding and §4.4. The task's initial free\nenvironment travels **once, explicitly**, as the root's `free-env`\nslot, a `:bindings` row (`[S V …]` sorted). Every `E` in the task is a\ncomplete map and is checked by rules X1 and E2. On lower, the\nsemantic-register kernel receives it as the machine's base `:env`\n(`create-vm`'s `:env` option, `semantic_register.cljc:261`); a de Bruijn\nkernel receives it as its `:free-env` (`stack.cljc:418`) and\nreconstructs positional frames from each `E` by the chain (§4.4).\n\n**Where the lift gets it (PROPOSED, the gap the review named).** It is\n**never recovered from a current `E`** (§4.4). Its source is, per\nkernel:\n\n- **de Bruijn kernels**: the kernel's own `:free-env` field, \"fixed for\n  this instance\" (`stack.cljc:82`; `register.cljc:50`), read directly.\n- **the semantic-register kernel**: the evaluator keeps only the\n  mutable-current `:env` (`RegisterVM` field `env`, \"persistent lexical\n  scope map\", `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:23`; the old semantic\n  VM likewise captures the initial env only transiently in `eval`,\n  `semantic.cljc:874-876`), so no field holds the initial map. The\n  **composition owns it**: it is the value the composition passed as\n  `create-vm`'s `:env` (`vm/check-bindings!` of it, `:261`). The lift's\n  input contract therefore takes it explicitly,\n  `(rows/lift-task vm serve! {:free-env E₀})`, and refuses\n  `:yin.k/non-portable :missing-free-env` when the caller supplies none;\n  the holder and REPL paths that call the lift pass the environment they\n  constructed the task with. **Coordinated retention seam, recommended**:\n  4b (stage 3, its track's file) adds an immutable `free-env` field set\n  once in `create-vm` from the checked `:env` and never written by any\n  transition, with `gc-roots` listing it; once it lands the lift reads\n  it when `:free-env` is not supplied and the explicit argument stays as\n  the override for compositions that constructed the task elsewhere.\n  Phase 6 does **not** edit `semantic_register.cljc`; 6b depends on the\n  explicit argument and names the seam as a follow-up (§8.2).\n\nMerkle sharing means every `E` whose bindings equal another's shares one\n`:bindings` row; the root slot is one more reference to a row that\nusually already exists.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Lift and lower\n\n### 7.1 Lift\n\n**DECIDED** (draft §9, UCF §7.8): refuse unless quiescent; refuse the\nholds (`unliftable-hold`, `handoff.cljc:588`) as `:yin.k/non-portable\n:reason-mismatch`; classify kind; run the **dependency closure over the\n`\"v4\"` vectors**, which needs the phase-5 scanners\n(`scan/requirements`, `scan/free-names`, `scan/free-occurrences` over the\n§2.3 table: the current `completion/code-facts` reads stack-table\npositions and cannot be used), and refuse `:yin.k/unsatisfied` unless\n`:complete`, `:yin.k/trees` included; number cursor cells (draft §6); walk\nwaits, parked records, the store slice, module stores, the free\nenvironment (from the kernel's `:free-env` field or the lift's explicit\n`:free-env` argument, §6.3, never from a current `E`), the result,\ninstall children; run `frame/defect` over every\nframe; emit rows and the census. A de Bruijn source walks the frames\n`layout/lift-act`/`lift-tail` reconstruct.\n\n### 7.2 Lower\n\n**DECIDED** (draft §8 in order; §3.3): gate, structure, graph, hashes,\ncanonical form, canonical numbering, **frames**, pending and operations,\ndependency closure (`requires`/`code` agree with the census;\n`:yin.k/trees` complete per §6.1), custody, composition, restore. Restore\nbuilds the receiving kernel's state: semantic-register: `code` through\n`load-vector`/`attach-image` under `code/contract`, the free environment\nas base `:env`, each `:wait` to an engine entry (payload plus the\npending's engine fields, `lower-frame!`'s shapes, `handoff.cljc:3182-3246`,\n`:deliver` carried), parked records into `:parked`, the result into\n`:value`; de Bruijn: derive and attach the image for each A, set\n`:free-env`, and `layout/lower-act`/`lower-tail` each frame (the stack\nlane's `tail` needs 6c-pre). Restoration delivers nothing, runs nothing,\nmints nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Slices, gates, entry conditions\n\nVerification follows `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`: G0 per iteration on\nthe JVM, G1 `bb test:sub yin.vm` on three hosts, G2 `bb test:changed`,\nG3 on master.\n\n### 8.1 Slice 6a: the frame validator and the row codec (independent)\n\n**Files to create.**\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc` (§3): `defect`, public.\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (§2): the row table as data,\n  `frame->rows`, `rows->frame`, row ids (Jing default), the census and\n  numbering per the draft §6, `canonical-under` (§5.5, test-only but\n  placed here so three test namespaces share it). **Not** `lift-task`/\n  `lower-task`: full task transport is 6b.\n- `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc`,\n  `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc`.\n\n**Depends on:** phase 3, 4a (landed), 4b stage 1 (branch) for live\nframes to validate. Touches nothing of 4b or 5; needs no scanner.\n\n**Acceptance (6a).**\n\n1. `frame-test/contract-is-pure`: `frame/defect` takes `[frame code\n   context task]`, `task` being plain data; the namespace's `ns` form\n   requires no kernel and no `yin.vm.engine` (a string check over the\n   source on the JVM lane, `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`).\n2. `frame-test/every-reference-frame-validates`: for every 4b-stage-1\n   row of §5.2 (1, 2, 5, 6, 13-16, 18, 19, 21, 22) over the four segments,\n   plus row 20 as one separate, unwrapped run (its empty `K` needs no wrapper\n   frames; §8.2 6b makes the same exception), every\n   `act`, `tail`, return frame, parked record and reified value the\n   register evaluator mints passes `defect` in its context with the\n   task context decoded from the machine's own tables.\n3. `frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper`: for each rule S1-S4, C1-C3,\n   A1-A6, T1, K1-K3, E1-E2, X1, P1-P4 one tampered frame built from a\n   valid one, refused with that rule's kind and a path naming the slot\n   (**twenty-four rules**: 4+3+6+1+3+2+1+4, the twenty-three of the\n   round-1 text plus X1; **twenty-five rows**, since C2 contributes two,\n   a float `pc` for `:pc-kind` and an out-of-range one for `:pc-bounds`;\n   X1's row goes through `frame/task-defect`); plus\n   `first-defect-is-structural`: a frame with a malformed `K` **and** a\n   bad window reports `:k-shape`.\n4. `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member`: row 22's frame\n   validates with the nil key present; the same frame with the key\n   removed is `:window-missing`.\n5. `frame-test/worked-example-saved`: on `:worked-example`, a frame at pc\n   4 with window `{1 <f>}` and `rd 2` validates; `{1 <f> 2 x}` is\n   `:window-self`; `{}` is `:window-missing`; `{1 <f> 3 x}` is\n   `:window-extra` (`saved(4, 2) = {1}`, `analysis_test.cljc:131-139`).\n6. `frame-test/free-env-mismatch`: row 21's frame (initial free\n   environment `{x 99 y 7}`) with `task :free-env {x 99 y 7}` validates;\n   with the free environment `{x 99 y 8}` or `{x 99}` it is\n   `:free-env-mismatch` (`y` is unshadowed); with the lexical `x` removed\n   from `E` it is `:free-env-mismatch` (presence); changing the lexical\n   `x` in `E` from `1` to `98` **does not** trip E2 (it is off the\n   comparison), and the test asserts that too; a `free-env` row with the\n   key `yin/def` is `:reserved-name` (X1).\n7. `rows-test/bijection`: `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame` and the converse\n   are identities on every frame of item 2, nil-valued keys included.\n8. `rows-test/row-ids-are-jing-default`: every content row's id equals\n   `(jing/segment-key body)` and names Jing's default algorithm; no\n   `sha256` appears in any id.\n9. `rows-test/window-sorted-and-unique`: an out-of-order or duplicated\n   `:window` row is `:yin.k/undecodable` at canonical form (step 5).\n10. `rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`: §5.5's\n    transformation gives equal root ids for two emissions of one abstract\n    task under permuted cursor-cell numbering and distinct stream identities,\n    with the fixture's correspondence map; **and the unordered-container\n    permutation**: a store value that is a set of two stream references\n    and a map keyed by two cursor references, emitted twice with the two\n    streams' identities swapped (and the correspondence map swapped\n    accordingly), gives equal root ids; a marker absent from the map is\n    a test failure.\n11. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log\n    shows `Testing yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test` and\n    `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`.\n12. `rows-test/discovery-order-numbering`: `canonical-numbering` returns\n    the maps of the numbering note's appendix A for `fixture :s1 :s2 :x\n    :y`, the review counterexample, `[x x y]`, `[x y y]`, `[#{X Y} X]`,\n    the witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]`, `[#{X Y} #{Y Z}]`, the path and\n    the two frame fixtures.\n13. `rows-test/occurrence-count-separates-members`: the review\n    counterexample numbers `Y cc-1, X cc-2`, pinned `2d9873a8…`; the path\n    pinned `726a9fbb…`; `[#{X Y} #{Y Z}]` pinned `d84480d4…`; each equal\n    after renaming plus reversal of every set.\n14. `rows-test/interchangeable-ties`: `#{X Y}`, `#{[X X] [Y Y]}`,\n    `{X 1, Y 1}`, `#{#{X Y} #{Z W}}` number without refusal; reversal and\n    renaming give equal roots; pins `07eda35d…`, `da69c679…`,\n    `49d4478c…`, `18b70de6…`.\n15. `rows-test/alias-pattern-is-part-of-the-key`: `#{[X X] [Y Z]}` and\n    `{X X, Y Z}` give one root for both enumerations and after renaming,\n    pinned `387f294a…` and `be62ba43…`; the witness numbers `B cc-1,\n    A cc-2`, pinned `0193312…`, and decodes; the balanced-alias witness\n    `#{[X X Y Y] [Z W Z W]}` gives one root for both enumerations, pinned\n    `5376f133…`, and the key without the local index would not.\n16. `rows-test/unresolved-cursor-cells-refuse`: the 2-cycle, the\n    3-cycle, the loop plus 2-cycle, the seven-cell state,\n    `[#{X Y} #{X Y}]`, the mixed-body, the anchored, the two-2-cycle and\n    the 3-cycle-beside-fan states refuse at `emit` with\n    `:yin.k/non-portable :unresolved-cursor-cells`, the paths and cells of\n    the numbering note's appendix A, the same verdict and path after\n    renaming plus shuffling; a carrier of each built with `emit-numbered`\n    decodes to `:yin.k/undecodable :unresolved-cursor-cells` with the\n    path prefixed by the root, never `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`; a\n    parent whose install `'a` holds the 2-cycle refuses at `emit` with\n    path `[12 a 15]` and its `emit-numbered` carrier decodes to the\n    `:yin.k/undecodable` kind with path `[<root> 12 a 15]`.\n17. `rows-test/canonical-roots-are-pinned`: `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n    unchanged; `a850fce6…` (`[#{X Y} X]`), `4993b5b1…`, `536c810b…`,\n    `e67405ec…` (`[#{#{X Y} #{Z W}} X]`), `6e7c7a6b…` (ten cells) added;\n    `55ff168e…` removed.\n18. `rows-test/counterexample-search`: a seeded generator (at least 2000\n    random value states, 200 frame-bearing, 100 with install children)\n    in CI: every numbered state's carrier decodes and re-emits to its\n    root; renaming every cursor cell plus shuffling every set, map and\n    census gives an equal root, or the same refusal verdict and path;\n    refusals are counted and reported; the largest `:work` is reported.\n19. `rows-test/numbering-is-total`: a census cell the walk does not reach\n    raises the totality defect, not a refusal, before any row is emitted.\n20. `numbering-precedes-frame-defect`, `alias-topology-and-census`,\n    `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`,\n    `unordered-containers-are-order-free`,\n    `child-scope-and-shared-child-dag` and\n    `census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` pass unchanged against the\n    rewritten decoder; `numbering-precedes-frame-defect` is extended: the\n    2-cycle with the same reserved-name binding, carried by\n    `emit-numbered`, decodes to `:yin.k/undecodable\n    :unresolved-cursor-cells`, not `:reserved-name`.\n21. `rows-test/gates-and-work`: 65 cells refuse `:resource-limit\n    [:cursor-cells]` under the default budget and 2 cells under\n    `{:cursor-cells 1}`; `[[[[X]]]]` under `{:depth 3}` refuses\n    `[:depth]`, and so do one cell inside 3000 nested vectors under\n    `{:depth 3}` and under the default budget, and a literal nested 3000\n    deep beside a cell (no host stack overflow on any of the three hosts;\n    200 nested vectors number); a set holding a 400000-scalar literal\n    refuses `[:work]` under `{:work 2000}` with the work counter at 2001\n    and under `{:work 900000}` with at most 1000 estimator steps; a state\n    whose bodies carry a 65536-character descriptor numbers under the\n    default budget; `{:work 1}` refuses `[:work]` at `emit` and, for a\n    valid carrier, at `decode`.\n22. Budgets: `:label-bytes` and `:search` gone, `:work` default\n    `4194304`.\n\n### 8.2 Slice 6b: full task transport and the harness on the reference lane\n\n**Files to change.** `rows.cljc`: `lift-task`, `lower-task` (§7), the\npending rows' lift and lower, install children. **Files to create.**\n`test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (§5, the\n`:semantic-register` lane). The old harness file is not edited.\n\n**Depends on:** the explicit `:free-env` lift argument supplied by the\nharness (§6.3; the 4b retention seam is a named follow-up for the 4b\ntrack, not a 6b prerequisite); 4b stage 2 (FFI retained→sent restoration, link\nrequest/response/install preservation, install children, the\nevaluator's `IModuleKernel` linking methods: `link-format`,\n`spawn-module`, `lift-closure`, `lower-closure`); **phase 5c** (the\n`scan` namespace, for the dependency closure over `\"v4\"` vectors, §7.1).\nTouches nothing of 4b or 5.\n\n**Acceptance (6b).**\n\n1. `every-row-every-segment-matches-the-reference`: rows 1-19, 21, 22\n   and 24 of §5.2 × four segments, plus row 20 once (outside the\n   wrappers, §5.2), on the reference lane; laws 1-3 and 6; counts\n   asserted (22 wrapped rows × 4 segments + 1 = 89 runs).\n2. `tail-states-carry-no-window`: rows 6, 9, 12, 20 lift to `:tail`\n   rows of three slots and lower to through-`K` delivery.\n3. `install-rows-carry-the-child`: rows 10-12; the child's kind and\n   phase as stated; no initialization on lower.\n4. `captures`: rows 14-16 round-trip; row 15's invocation after lower\n   delivers once into the captured `rd` and yields `:done`.\n5. `free-env-shadowing`: row 21 yields `99` after lower.\n6. `synthetic-tail-bookkeeping`: row 23's hand-built parked `tail`\n   under a call id in `:ffi-call-ids` passes `defect` with context\n   `:parked`; the **same valid record under a key absent from\n   `:ffi-call-ids`** is `:parked-site` (P4); the record with `site` moved\n   to a non-tail call is `:site` (T1 runs before P4).\n7. `refusals`: every refusal row of §5.2 refuses with the named status\n   and kind before any attachment; `first-defect-order`: a body with a\n   noncanonical cursor-cell numbering **and** a tampered window reports\n   `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`.\n8. `a-response-cursor-shared-by-two-waiters-crosses-as-one-cursor-cell` and\n   `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`, ported.\n9. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n\n### 8.3 Slice 6c: the layouts, the stack seam, the cross-engine lanes\n\n**6c-pre, the stack tail-completion seam.** File to change:\n`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc` (§4.3): park-entry builders mark a\ntail-call park `:resume-mode :return-result`; `stack-restore` delivers\nsuch an entry by the return transition. Test to create:\n`test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_tail_completion_test.cljc`: a tail\neffectful call parked and resumed delivers through `K` (pops the frame,\ntruncates to its base, pushes the value) and halts with the value when\n`K` is empty; a tail call in operand position never executes the layout\nsyntax after it; non-tail parks are unchanged (the old stack tests stay\ngreen). **Depends on** nothing of 4b or 5.\n\n**6c proper.** Files to create: `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc`\n(§4); `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc`; the two extra\nlanes added to the 6b harness file. **Depends on:** 5a, 5b (`derive`),\n6b, 6c-pre.\n\n**Acceptance (6c).**\n\n1. `layout-test/register-pairing`: for every `P ∈ C`, `phys` is total on\n   every body's named virtuals; `virt(p, s)` is single-valued at every\n   reachable boundary pc (§5.6 item 3).\n2. `layout-test/register-live-is-live-out`: §5.6 item 3's second clause,\n   tail boundaries `[]`.\n3. `layout-test/register-rd-from-a`: on `:worked-example`'s register\n   lane at the inner call's park, the canonical `rd` is `2` while the\n   kernel's `dest` is `3`; the K frame of a nested non-tail call in\n   `:depth-3` has its `rd` from A, not its physical `dest`.\n4. `layout-test/stack-correspondence`: §5.6 item 4.\n5. `layout-test/stack-layout-is-the-saved-set`: §5.6 item 5 and the\n   worked cases: `(f (g x) y)` at the inner call → `[1]`; `(f (if c (g)\n   2) y)` at `(g)` → `[1]`.\n6. `layout-test/stack-slices-partition`: §5.6 item 9; and the\n   multi-frame fixture, the expression `(cat [1] ((fn [x] (cat [2] ((fn\n   [y] (cat [3] (next-of c))) 2))) 1))` under the harness's standard\n   binding setup: `with-cat` outermost, then `(let1 s (stream/make 4)\n   (let1 c (cursor-of s) …))` around it (the stream is made inside the\n   program, as every row does: that is this fixture's chosen setup. A\n   primitive `cat` supplied in the free environment would sit in a live\n   slot and is no carrier value, `:continuation-registers`,\n   `debruijn_register_effects.cljc:196`; an authentic cursor reference is\n   machine data with an explicit carrier marker, `engine.cljc:899-905`, so\n   in-program construction of `c` is a fixture choice, not a carrier\n   restriction). **Derivation of the expression\n   alone** (`cat` and `c` taken as given): the outer application of\n   `(fn [x] …)` pops its closure and `1`, leaving the outer `cat` and\n   `[1]` pushed, so its frame's base is `2`; the inner application leaves\n   the middle `cat` and `[2]` as well, base `4`; the current activation\n   has pushed its `cat` and `[3]` and the read has popped its cursor\n   operand (`stack.cljc:839`), so the operand stack has six values:\n   slices `[0,2)` = `[cat [1]]`, `[2,4)` = `[cat [2]]`, current `[4,6)` =\n   `[cat [3]]`, each slice's `stack-layout` being `[operator-rd\n   literal-rd]` of its `cat` call and equal to that activation's saved\n   window. **As run**, the three binding applications each pop their\n   closure and single operand off an otherwise empty stack, so `K` has\n   **five** frames with bases `0, 0, 0, 2, 4`, slices `[0,0) [0,0) [0,0)\n   [0,2) [2,4)`, current `[4,6)`, stack length six; the test pins these\n   bases from the kernel's state, checks the partition, and checks that\n   lowering the lifted frame emits the same five bases (§4.3; the\n   before-slice rule would emit `0, 0, 0, 0, 2`).\n7. `layout-test/env-reconstruction`: §5.6 item 6.\n8. `layout-test/closures-round-trip`: §5.6 item 7.\n9. `layout-test/tail-lowering-is-unobservable`: §5.6 item 8.\n10. `harness/cross-engine-canonical-equality`: law 4 for every row ×\n    segment under `canonical-under`.\n11. `harness/cross-engine-lowering`: law 5, six ordered pairs.\n12. `harness/layout-refusals`: `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` from a kernel\n    stepped to a non-safepoint pc; a register entry whose `live` was\n    tampered reconstructs a frame the validator refuses (`:window-extra`\n    or `:window-missing` by the tamper's direction).\n13. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n\n### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n\n**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 7). 6a-6c green on three hosts; the row\ncarrier the only writer and reader the semantic-register kernel has; a\ndocumented seam for the holder, checkpoint, ledger and authority paths\n(phase 7 wires it; phase 6 edits none of them); the Stage D/E scenarios\n(`stage_e_scenarios.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`) listed with, for\neach, the §5.2 row that exercises its parking shape; the export-recovery\nobject (UCF §7.7.4, format version 1 over the old codec) re-based on the\nrow carrier by phase 7, since it embeds a body; and the free-environment\nretention seam (§6.3) either landed by the 4b track or the explicit\n`:free-env` argument threaded through the holder's export path.\n\n### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n\n| | needs | concurrent with |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n\nNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\nregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are","numLines":380,"startLine":979,"totalLines":1762}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ChJzLx6y7tvT9GX7c2nL1N","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
