{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VQRxkfxw3AkjbfW9R9uUkq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis\n2\t  \"Static facts per pc derived from A\n3\t   (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §8.1): per body, the\n4\t   explicit control-flow graph, `def`, `use`, the live-in set `L` by\n5\t   backward liveness to a fixed point, and the saved-window rule\n6\t   `saved(p, rd) = L(p) − {rd}`.\n7\t\n8\t   Pure functions of a vector that passed\n9\t   `yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`. Nothing here is persisted\n10\t   in A; a receiver recomputes it from the vector alone.\"\n11\t  (:require [clojure.set :as set]\n12\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]))\n13\t\n14\t\n15\t(defn successors\n16\t  \"§8.1's successor relation for the instruction at `pc`: none for\n17\t   `:return`, `:halt`, `:resume` and a tail `:call` (runtime\n18\t   terminators); the target for `:jump`; `pc+1` and the target for\n19\t   `:branch-false`; `pc+1` otherwise. Every edge stays inside the body\n20\t   (§3.4 item 6).\"\n21\t  [v pc]\n22\t  (let [t (nth v pc)]\n23\t    (case (nth t 0)\n24\t      (:return :halt :resume) []\n25\t      :jump [(nth t 1)]\n26\t      :branch-false [(inc pc) (nth t 2)]\n27\t      :call (if (code/tail-call? t) [] [(inc pc)])\n28\t      [(inc pc)])))\n29\t\n30\t\n31\t(defn defs\n32\t  \"`def(pc)`: `#{rd}` for an instruction with a destination slot, `#{}`\n33\t   otherwise. A tail `:call` names its `rd` and has no successor, so its\n34\t   `def` never reaches an `L`.\"\n35\t  [v pc]\n36\t  (if-let [r (code/rd (nth v pc))] #{r} #{}))\n37\t\n38\t\n39\t(defn uses\n40\t  \"`use(pc)`: the instruction's register operands, as a set.\"\n41\t  [v pc]\n42\t  (set (code/uses (nth v pc))))\n43\t\n44\t\n45\t(defn- body-live\n46\t  \"Backward liveness over one body `[start, end)` to a fixed point:\n47\t   `L(p) = use(p) ∪ (⋃ L(s) for s in succ(p)) − def(p)`, swept in\n48\t   decreasing pc order until no set changes. Returns a vector of sets\n49\t   indexed by `pc - start`.\"\n50\t  [v start end]\n51\t  (let [ps (range (dec end) (dec start) -1)\n52\t        du (mapv (fn [pc] [(uses v pc) (defs v pc) (successors v pc)])\n53\t                 (range start end))]\n54\t    (loop [live (vec (repeat (- end start) #{}))]\n55\t      (let [swept (reduce (fn [live pc]\n56\t                            (let [[u d ss] (nth du (- pc start))\n57\t                                  out (reduce (fn [acc s]\n58\t                                                (into acc\n59\t                                                      (nth live (- s start))))\n60\t                                              #{}\n61\t                                              ss)]\n62\t                              (assoc live\n63\t                                     (- pc start)\n64\t                                     (into u (set/difference out d)))))\n65\t                          live\n66\t                          ps)]\n67\t        (if (= swept live) live (recur swept))))))\n68\t\n69\t\n70\t(defn analyze\n71\t  \"The §8.1 facts of a well-formed vector. Returns `{:bodies [{:start s\n72\t   :end e} …] :successors [succ …] :def [set …] :use [set …] :live [set\n73\t   …]}`, the last four indexed by pc, `:live` being `L` computed per\n74\t   body over the stated edges, so instructions unreachable from a\n75\t   terminal path (layout syntax) have an `L` like any other node.\"\n76\t  [v]\n77\t  (let [bodies (mapv #(select-keys % [:start :end]) (code/body-ranges v))]\n78\t    {:bodies bodies,\n79\t     :successors (mapv #(successors v %) (range (count v))),\n80\t     :def (mapv #(defs v %) (range (count v))),\n81\t     :use (mapv #(uses v %) (range (count v))),\n82\t     :live (into [] (mapcat (fn [{:keys [start end]}] (body-live v start end)))\n83\t                 bodies)}))\n84\t\n85\t\n86\t(defn live\n87\t  \"`L(p)` from an `analyze` result.\"\n88\t  [analysis p]\n89\t  (nth (:live analysis) p))\n90\t\n91\t\n92\t(defn saved\n93\t  \"The saved-window rule (§2.4, §8.1): the registers a frame, wait,\n94\t   parked record or capture resuming at `p` with delivery `{:deliver :rd\n95\t   :rd rd}` carries, `L(p) − {rd}`. The subtraction is explicit.\"\n96\t  [analysis p rd]\n97\t  (disj (live analysis p) rd))\n98\t\n99\t\n100\t(defn reachable\n101\t  \"The pcs reachable from the start of the body holding `pc`, over the\n102\t   stated successor edges.\"\n103\t  [v pc]\n104\t  (let [bodies (code/body-ranges v)\n105\t        start (:start (nth bodies (code/body-index bodies pc)))]\n106\t    (loop [seen #{start}\n107\t           todo [start]]\n108\t      (if-let [p (peek todo)]\n109\t        (let [fresh (remove seen (successors v p))]\n110\t          (recur (into seen fresh) (into (pop todo) fresh)))\n111\t        seen))))\n112\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b921a1a6-65e4-4bc4-853c-fc87c8b912fe","uuid":"1c05d6bd-147c-4330-9ecb-deb15e1ecbf5","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:42:24.878Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/analysis.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis\n  \"Static facts per pc derived from A\n   (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §8.1): per body, the\n   explicit control-flow graph, `def`, `use`, the live-in set `L` by\n   backward liveness to a fixed point, and the saved-window rule\n   `saved(p, rd) = L(p) − {rd}`.\n\n   Pure functions of a vector that passed\n   `yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`. Nothing here is persisted\n   in A; a receiver recomputes it from the vector alone.\"\n  (:require [clojure.set :as set]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]))\n\n\n(defn successors\n  \"§8.1's successor relation for the instruction at `pc`: none for\n   `:return`, `:halt`, `:resume` and a tail `:call` (runtime\n   terminators); the target for `:jump`; `pc+1` and the target for\n   `:branch-false`; `pc+1` otherwise. Every edge stays inside the body\n   (§3.4 item 6).\"\n  [v pc]\n  (let [t (nth v pc)]\n    (case (nth t 0)\n      (:return :halt :resume) []\n      :jump [(nth t 1)]\n      :branch-false [(inc pc) (nth t 2)]\n      :call (if (code/tail-call? t) [] [(inc pc)])\n      [(inc pc)])))\n\n\n(defn defs\n  \"`def(pc)`: `#{rd}` for an instruction with a destination slot, `#{}`\n   otherwise. A tail `:call` names its `rd` and has no successor, so its\n   `def` never reaches an `L`.\"\n  [v pc]\n  (if-let [r (code/rd (nth v pc))] #{r} #{}))\n\n\n(defn uses\n  \"`use(pc)`: the instruction's register operands, as a set.\"\n  [v pc]\n  (set (code/uses (nth v pc))))\n\n\n(defn- body-live\n  \"Backward liveness over one body `[start, end)` to a fixed point:\n   `L(p) = use(p) ∪ (⋃ L(s) for s in succ(p)) − def(p)`, swept in\n   decreasing pc order until no set changes. Returns a vector of sets\n   indexed by `pc - start`.\"\n  [v start end]\n  (let [ps (range (dec end) (dec start) -1)\n        du (mapv (fn [pc] [(uses v pc) (defs v pc) (successors v pc)])\n                 (range start end))]\n    (loop [live (vec (repeat (- end start) #{}))]\n      (let [swept (reduce (fn [live pc]\n                            (let [[u d ss] (nth du (- pc start))\n                                  out (reduce (fn [acc s]\n                                                (into acc\n                                                      (nth live (- s start))))\n                                              #{}\n                                              ss)]\n                              (assoc live\n                                     (- pc start)\n                                     (into u (set/difference out d)))))\n                          live\n                          ps)]\n        (if (= swept live) live (recur swept))))))\n\n\n(defn analyze\n  \"The §8.1 facts of a well-formed vector. Returns `{:bodies [{:start s\n   :end e} …] :successors [succ …] :def [set …] :use [set …] :live [set\n   …]}`, the last four indexed by pc, `:live` being `L` computed per\n   body over the stated edges, so instructions unreachable from a\n   terminal path (layout syntax) have an `L` like any other node.\"\n  [v]\n  (let [bodies (mapv #(select-keys % [:start :end]) (code/body-ranges v))]\n    {:bodies bodies,\n     :successors (mapv #(successors v %) (range (count v))),\n     :def (mapv #(defs v %) (range (count v))),\n     :use (mapv #(uses v %) (range (count v))),\n     :live (into [] (mapcat (fn [{:keys [start end]}] (body-live v start end)))\n                 bodies)}))\n\n\n(defn live\n  \"`L(p)` from an `analyze` result.\"\n  [analysis p]\n  (nth (:live analysis) p))\n\n\n(defn saved\n  \"The saved-window rule (§2.4, §8.1): the registers a frame, wait,\n   parked record or capture resuming at `p` with delivery `{:deliver :rd\n   :rd rd}` carries, `L(p) − {rd}`. The subtraction is explicit.\"\n  [analysis p rd]\n  (disj (live analysis p) rd))\n\n\n(defn reachable\n  \"The pcs reachable from the start of the body holding `pc`, over the\n   stated successor edges.\"\n  [v pc]\n  (let [bodies (code/body-ranges v)\n        start (:start (nth bodies (code/body-index bodies pc)))]\n    (loop [seen #{start}\n           todo [start]]\n      (if-let [p (peek todo)]\n        (let [fresh (remove seen (successors v p))]\n          (recur (into seen fresh) (into (pop todo) fresh)))\n        seen))))\n","numLines":112,"startLine":1,"totalLines":112}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VQRxkfxw3AkjbfW9R9uUkq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
