{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MeT21B4uxPHXaEAaY6JyHn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.debruijn.register\n2\t  \"R4 (docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md S5, S6 R4): the register\n3\t   execution kernel that interprets positional register images\n4\t   `{:bodies [...], :instructions [...]}` under contract version 4\n5\t   (the \\\"r2\\\" contract).\n6\t\n7\t   The register kernel is a sibling to `yin.vm.debruijn.stack` (B3/B4) and\n8\t   `yin.vm.semantic`. It preserves B3's frame direction, closure capture,\n9\t   nil-fill and extra-argument rules, and B0 normalization. It executes\n10\t   only validator-approved images.\n11\t\n12\t   State: `{:segment :hash :images :pc :frames :free-env :registers\n13\t            :continuation :store :blocked? :halted? :wait-set :ready-queue\n14\t            :parked :id-counter :value :make-stream :bridge :primitives\n15\t            :modules}`.\n16\t\n17\t   Continuation transport: register continuations and stack continuations\n18\t   are not interchangeable (section 5.1). Payloads carry `:format\n19\t   :yin.debruijn.register`, `:hash R` of the code space at the time, and\n20\t   `:image`, the offset-table row their pc falls in (yin.vm.linker.md\n21\t   section 7.3, r6). A foreign format or an `:image` the table does not\n22\t   hold is refused with qualified `:continuation-format` diagnostics.\n23\t   Resume values must be plain data, refusing host exceptions with\n24\t   `:resume-value`.\n25\t\n26\t   The kernel implements all 23 opcodes, Rule R's `:define` included,\n27\t   across the pure-program tier and the\n28\t   effects tier, connecting to `yin.vm.engine` via `register-restore` and\n29\t   per-site wait-entry builders.\"\n30\t  (:require [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n31\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n32\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n33\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-effects :as effects]\n34\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n35\t            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n36\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n37\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n38\t\n39\t\n40\t;; =============================================================================\n41\t;; State\n42\t;; =============================================================================\n43\t\n44\t(defrecord DebruijnRegisterVM\n45\t  [segment      ; {:bodies [...], :instructions [...]}\n46\t   hash         ; R of segment (yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash)\n47\t   images       ; offset table: [[identity offset length] ...], base first\n48\t   pc           ; program counter into :instructions\n49\t   frames       ; positional lexical frame stack, outermost first\n50\t   free-env     ; initial free-name environment map\n51\t   registers    ; persistent vector for current body's register file\n52\t   continuation ; vector of return frames (innermost last)\n53\t   store        ; heap map\n54\t   blocked?     ; engine: boolean\n55\t   halted?      ; engine: boolean\n56\t   wait-set     ; engine: vector of wait entries\n57\t   ready-queue  ; engine: vector of woken entries\n58\t   parked       ; engine: map of parked continuations\n59\t   id-counter   ; engine: counter for gensym, stream, and park ids\n60\t   value        ; engine: last computed value\n61\t   make-stream  ; host stream constructor or nil\n62\t   bridge       ; host FFI bridge or nil\n63\t   primitives   ; primitive registry for :load-free\n64\t   modules      ; module registry for :load-free and effect dispatch\n65\t   store-of     ; the running body's module store address, or nil\n66\t   resources    ; private engine resources: the link pair\n67\t   origin       ; this task's origin tag for link ids\n68\t   ancestry     ; the modules installing on this task's install chain\n69\t   gc])         ; {:since :base :threshold :pinned}: heap reclamation\n70\t\n71\t\n72\t(def format-tag\n73\t  \"The model tag every register payload carries as `:format`.\"\n74\t  effects/format-tag)\n75\t\n76\t\n77\t;; =============================================================================\n78\t;; Body & frame addressing\n79\t;; =============================================================================\n80\t\n81\t(defn- body-of-pc\n82\t  \"Return the declared body map covering instruction `pc` in `segment`.\"\n83\t  [{:keys [bodies]} pc]\n84\t  (some (fn [{:keys [start end] :as body}]\n85\t          (when (and (<= start pc) (<= pc end)) body))\n86\t        bodies))\n87\t\n88\t\n89\t(defn- frame-value\n90\t  \"Frame 0 for `:load-bound` is the INNERMOST frame, read from the END of\n91\t   `:frames`. `frames` is outermost-first, so depth `d` is\n92\t   `(count frames) - 1 - d`.\"\n93\t  [frames depth position]\n94\t  (let [n (count frames)\n95\t        idx (- n 1 depth)]\n96\t    (when (or (neg? idx) (>= idx n))\n97\t      (throw (ex-info \"load-bound: depth out of range\"\n98\t                      {:rule :load-bound-depth, :depth depth,\n99\t                       :frame-count n})))\n100\t    (let [frame (nth frames idx)]\n101\t      (when (or (neg? position) (>= position (count frame)))\n102\t        (throw (ex-info \"load-bound: position out of range\"\n103\t                        {:rule :load-bound-position, :depth depth,\n104\t                         :position position, :frame-arity (count frame)})))\n105\t      (nth frame position))))\n106\t\n107\t\n108\t(defn- bind-positional\n109\t  \"Positional parameter binding: missing arguments are nil-filled,\n110\t   extra arguments dropped.\"\n111\t  [arity args]\n112\t  (vec (take arity (concat args (repeat nil)))))\n113\t\n114\t\n115\t;; =============================================================================\n116\t;; Image loading & VM construction\n117\t;; =============================================================================\n118\t\n119\t(defn- empty-segment?\n120\t  [segment]\n121\t  (or (nil? segment)\n122\t      (empty? segment)\n123\t      (and (map? segment) (empty? (:instructions segment)))))\n124\t\n125\t\n126\t(def ^:private empty-image {:bodies [], :instructions []})\n127\t\n128\t\n129\t(defn- install-image\n130\t  \"Install `segment` as the one image. A non-empty image must pass the\n131\t   register validator. The offset table restarts at the base row\n132\t   `[R 0 n]`.\"\n133\t  [vm segment]\n134\t  (let [empty-seg? (empty-segment? segment)]\n135\t    (if empty-seg?\n136\t      (assoc vm\n137\t             :segment empty-image\n138\t             :hash nil\n139\t             :images [[(rcode/register-hash empty-image) 0 0]]\n140\t             :pc 0\n141\t             :frames []\n142\t             :registers []\n143\t             :continuation []\n144\t             :halted? true\n145\t             :blocked? false\n146\t             :value nil)\n147\t      (if-let [defect (rcode/register-image-defect segment)]\n148\t        (throw (ex-info (str \"Invalid register image: \" (:rule defect))\n149\t                        defect))\n150\t        (let [body0 (first (:bodies segment))\n151\t              reg-count (or (:registers body0) 0)\n152\t              r (rcode/register-hash segment)]\n153\t          (assoc vm\n154\t                 :segment segment\n155\t                 :hash r\n156\t                 :images [[r 0 (count (:instructions segment))]]\n157\t                 :pc 0\n158\t                 :frames []\n159\t                 :registers (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n160\t                 :continuation []\n161\t                 :halted? false\n162\t                 :blocked? false\n163\t                 :value nil))))))\n164\t\n165\t\n166\t(defn load-image\n167\t  \"Load `segment` (a register image `{:bodies [...], :instructions [...]}`)\n168\t   into `vm` as its one image: R is computed, the registers are reset to\n169\t   pc 0 with empty frames and continuation, and the machine is running\n170\t   unless the segment is empty. The offset table restarts at `[R 0 n]`, so\n171\t   a continuation parked under an earlier image names no row of it and\n172\t   `register-restore` refuses it.\n173\t\n174\t   `contract` is required and compared with `vm/register-contract` first\n175\t   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`); a non-empty image must then\n176\t   pass the register validator, Rule R included. An empty segment admits\n177\t   no code and needs neither.\"\n178\t  [vm segment contract]\n179\t  (when-not (empty-segment? segment)\n180\t    (vm/check-contract! vm/register-contract contract))\n181\t  (install-image vm segment))\n182\t\n183\t\n184\t(defn relocate\n185\t  \"Shift every `:pc`-kind operand of `inst` by `offset`.\"\n186\t  [offset inst]\n187\t  (reduce (fn [inst [i [_ kind]]]\n188\t            (if (= :pc kind) (update inst (inc i) + offset) inst))\n189\t          inst\n190\t          (map-indexed vector (get rcode/opcode-table (nth inst 0)))))\n191\t\n192\t\n193\t(defn attach-image\n194\t  \"Extend the code space of `vm` with `image`, non-destructively\n195\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, act 3): `image` is admitted alone as\n196\t   `load-image` admits it, relocated by the held instruction count, and\n197\t   appended, `:bodies` shifted likewise; one `[identity offset length]`\n198\t   row, identity R of `image`, is appended to the offset table; `:hash`\n199\t   becomes R of the concatenation. `:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`,\n200\t   `:continuation`, and every other register are unchanged: appending\n201\t   moves no instruction already held. An image whose identity is already\n202\t   a row is not attached twice, and an empty image, which adds no code,\n203\t   is not attached at all.\"\n204\t  [vm image contract]\n205\t  (when-not (empty-segment? image)\n206\t    (vm/check-contract! vm/register-contract contract)\n207\t    (when-let [defect (rcode/register-image-defect image)]\n208\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"Invalid register image: \" (:rule defect))\n209\t                      defect))))\n210\t  (let [ident (when-not (empty-segment? image) (rcode/register-hash image))]\n211\t    (if (or (nil? ident) (some #(= ident (nth % 0)) (:images vm)))\n212\t      vm\n213\t      (let [held (:segment vm)\n214\t            offset (count (:instructions held))\n215\t            shift-body #(-> % (update :start + offset) (update :end + offset))\n216\t            combined {:bodies (into (:bodies held)\n217\t                                    (map shift-body)\n218\t                                    (:bodies image)),\n219\t                      :instructions (into (:instructions held)\n220\t                                          (map #(relocate offset %))\n221\t                                          (:instructions image))}]\n222\t        (assoc vm\n223\t               :segment combined\n224\t               :hash (rcode/register-hash combined)\n225\t               :images (conj (:images vm)\n226\t                             [ident offset\n227\t                              (count (:instructions image))]))))))\n228\t\n229\t\n230\t;; =============================================================================\n231\t;; Layouts: the ordered image list a code space is built from (UCF v2, 4.1)\n232\t;; =============================================================================\n233\t\n234\t(def max-layout-length\n235\t  \"2^52-1: the largest instruction-count sum a layout may name.\"\n236\t  4503599627370495)\n237\t\n238\t\n239\t(defn layout\n240\t  \"The ordered identities of `vm`'s offset table: its current layout.\"\n241\t  [vm]\n242\t  (mapv #(nth % 0) (:images vm)))\n243\t\n244\t\n245\t(defn compose\n246\t  \"The code space `images`, the component register images in layout\n247\t   order, build: `{:segment :hash :images}` where `:segment` is the\n248\t   relocated concatenation (bodies shifted likewise), `:images` the\n249\t   offset table derived by prefix sums, and `:hash` its R -- nil while\n250\t   no instruction is held, the empty base's convention.  A length sum\n251\t   beyond 2^52-1 refuses with `:layout-overflow`; nothing here validates\n252\t   an image.\"\n253\t  [images]\n254\t  (let [{:keys [bodies instructions rows]}\n255\t        (reduce (fn [{:keys [bodies instructions rows]} image]\n256\t                  (let [offset (count instructions)\n257\t                        n (count (:instructions image))]\n258\t                    (when (> (+ offset n) max-layout-length)\n259\t                      (throw (ex-info \"Layout length overflow\"\n260\t                                      {:rule :layout-overflow})))\n261\t                    {:bodies (into bodies\n262\t                                   (map #(-> %\n263\t                                             (update :start + offset)\n264\t                                             (update :end + offset)))\n265\t                                   (:bodies image))\n266\t                     :instructions (into instructions\n267\t                                         (map #(relocate offset %))\n268\t                                         (:instructions image))\n269\t                     :rows (conj rows [(rcode/register-hash image) offset n])}))\n270\t                {:bodies [] :instructions [] :rows []}\n271\t                images)\n272\t        segment {:bodies bodies :instructions instructions}]\n273\t    {:segment segment\n274\t     :hash (when (seq instructions) (rcode/register-hash segment))\n275\t     :images rows}))\n276\t\n277\t\n278\t(defn layout-images\n279\t  \"The component image of each row of the offset table `images` over\n280\t   `segment`, relocated back to its own pc 0, in table order; nil\n281\t   unless the table covers the segment exactly and every slice rehashes\n282\t   to its row's identity.\"\n283\t  [segment images]\n284\t  (when (and (map? segment) (nil? (effects/table-defect\n285\t                                    (count (:instructions segment)) images)))\n286\t    (let [slices (mapv #(effects/image-slice segment %) images)]\n287\t      (when (every? true?\n288\t                    (map (fn [[ident _ _] slice]\n289\t                           (= ident (rcode/register-hash slice)))\n290\t                         images slices))\n291\t        slices))))\n292\t\n293\t\n294\t(defn rebuild\n295\t  \"`vm` over the code space `images` (the component images in layout\n296\t   order) build, each non-empty one admitted alone under the register\n297\t   contract; the registers are reset.  The store, the parked map, the\n298\t   queues and the composition values survive.\"\n299\t  [vm images]\n300\t  (doseq [image images\n301\t          :when (not (empty-segment? image))]\n302\t    (when-let [defect (rcode/register-image-defect image)]\n303\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"Invalid register image: \" (:rule defect))\n304\t                      defect))))\n305\t  (let [{:keys [segment hash images]} (compose images)\n306\t        body0 (first (:bodies segment))]\n307\t    (assoc vm\n308\t           :segment segment\n309\t           :hash hash\n310\t           :images images\n311\t           :pc 0\n312\t           :frames []\n313\t           :registers (vec (repeat (or (:registers body0) 0) nil))\n314\t           :continuation []\n315\t           :store-of nil)))\n316\t\n317\t\n318\t(defn image-pc\n319\t  \"Lift an absolute `pc` of `vm` to `[identity rel-pc]` by its offset\n320\t   table, or nil when no row holds it.\"\n321\t  [vm pc]\n322\t  (when-let [[ident off] (effects/image-row (:images vm) pc)]\n323\t    [ident (- pc off)]))\n324\t\n325\t\n326\t(defn absolute-pc\n327\t  \"Lower `[identity rel-pc]` to an absolute pc of `vm` by its offset\n328\t   table, or nil when the identity is no row of it or `rel-pc` is no pc\n329\t   `image-pc` lifts into that row.\"\n330\t  [vm [ident rel-pc]]\n331\t  (let [images (:images vm)]\n332\t    (some (fn [[id off :as row]]\n333\t            (when (and (= id ident)\n334\t                       (nat-int? rel-pc)\n335\t                       (= row (effects/image-row images (+ off rel-pc))))\n336\t              (+ off rel-pc)))\n337\t          images)))\n338\t\n339\t\n340\t(defn create-vm\n341\t  \"Build a fresh `DebruijnRegisterVM` over `segment`.\n342\t   Options: `:free-env`, `:store`, `:primitives`, `:modules`, `:make-stream`,\n343\t   `:call-in`/`:call-out`/`:call-out-cursor`/`:ffi-caller-id`/\n344\t   `:call-capacity`, `:bridge`, and `:contract`, the\n345\t   segment's stamp, required when `segment` is non-empty (`load-image`). A\n346\t   `:free-env`, `:store`, or `:primitives` binding a reserved name is\n347\t   refused (Rule R). `:link-request`/`:link-response` (the link pair\n348\t   `require` lowers to), `:origin`, and `:ancestry` are\n349\t   `yin.vm/empty-state`'s.\"\n350\t  ([segment] (create-vm segment {}))\n351\t  ([segment opts]\n352\t   (let [base (vm/empty-state\n353\t                (assoc (select-keys opts [:modules :make-stream :call-in\n354\t                                          :call-out :call-out-cursor\n355\t                                          :ffi-caller-id :call-capacity\n356\t                                          :link-request :link-response\n357\t                                          :origin :ancestry\n358\t                                          :capability-secret :secret-source\n359\t                                          :attach-stream :gc-threshold])\n360\t                       :primitives (or (:primitives opts) {})))]\n361\t     (-> (map->DebruijnRegisterVM\n362\t           {:segment {:bodies [], :instructions []},\n363\t            :store-of nil,\n364\t            :resources (:resources base),\n365\t            :origin (:origin base),\n366\t            :ancestry (:ancestry base),\n367\t            :capability-secret (:capability-secret base),\n368\t            :owner (:owner base),\n369\t            :secret-source (:secret-source base),\n370\t            :attach-stream (:attach-stream base),\n371\t            :hash nil,\n372\t            :images [],\n373\t            :pc 0,\n374\t            :frames [],\n375\t            :free-env (vm/check-bindings! :env (or (:free-env opts) {})),\n376\t            :registers [],\n377\t            :continuation [],\n378\t            :store (merge (:store base)\n379\t                          (vm/check-bindings! :store (:store opts))),\n380\t            :blocked? false,\n381\t            :halted? true,\n382\t            :wait-set [],\n383\t            :ready-queue [],\n384\t            :parked {},\n385\t            :heap (:heap base),\n386\t            :gc (:gc base),\n387\t            :id-counter 0,\n388\t            :ffi-caller-id (:ffi-caller-id base),\n389\t            :value nil,\n390\t            :make-stream (:make-stream base),\n391\t            :bridge nil,\n392\t            :primitives (:primitives base),\n393\t            :callable-effects (:callable-effects base),\n394\t            :modules (or (:modules opts) {})})\n395\t         (load-image segment (:contract opts))\n396\t         (ffi/attach (:bridge opts))))))\n397\t\n398\t\n399\t;; =============================================================================\n400\t;; Return transitions & restore\n401\t;; =============================================================================\n402\t\n403\t(defn- return-transition\n404\t  \"Unified return transition: restores caller frame from continuation if\n405\t   pending, otherwise halts the VM with `val`. Only pc, frames, registers,\n406\t   and continuation are restored (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r7): a\n407\t   frame carries no code space, so an image attached while the call was\n408\t   in flight stays attached, and the absolute `:return-pc` still names\n409\t   the caller's instruction in the grown code space.\"\n410\t  [vm val]\n411\t  (let [continuation (:continuation vm)]\n412\t    (if (seq continuation)\n413\t      (let [frame (peek continuation)\n414\t            return-pc (:return-pc frame)\n415\t            body (body-of-pc (:segment vm) return-pc)\n416\t            reg-count (:registers body)\n417\t            dest (:dest frame)\n418\t            restored-regs (reduce (fn [acc [r v]] (assoc acc r v))\n419\t                                  (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n420\t                                  (:regs frame))\n421\t            final-regs (if (some? dest)\n422\t                         (assoc restored-regs dest val)\n423\t                         restored-regs)]\n424\t        (assoc vm\n425\t               :pc return-pc\n426\t               :frames (:frames frame)\n427\t               :registers final-regs\n428\t               :continuation (pop continuation)\n429\t               :store-of (:store-of frame)\n430\t               :value val\n431\t               :halted? false))\n432\t      (assoc vm :halted? true, :value val, :store-of nil))))\n433\t\n434\t\n435\t(defn- refuse-continuation!\n436\t  [base entry]\n437\t  (throw (ex-info \"Cannot restore a continuation of another model or image\"\n438\t                  {:reason :foreign-format,\n439\t                   :rule :continuation-format,\n440\t                   :format (:format entry),\n441\t                   :hash (:hash entry),\n442\t                   :image (:image entry),\n443\t                   :expected-format format-tag,\n444\t                   :expected-hash (:hash base),\n445\t                   :images (:images base)})))\n446\t\n447\t\n448\t(defn- check-format!\n449\t  \"Refuse `entry` unless it is this model's payload for a row of the offset\n450\t   table (r6).\"\n451\t  [base entry]\n452\t  (when-not (and (= format-tag (:format entry))\n453\t                 (some #(= (:image entry) (nth % 0)) (:images base)))\n454\t    (refuse-continuation! base entry)))\n455\t\n456\t\n457\t(defn- write-back\n458\t  \"Write `entry`'s registers back and deliver `val` via `:write-result` or\n459\t   `:return-result`. Registers only: `:segment` is kernel state.\"\n460\t  [base entry val]\n461\t  (if (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\n462\t    (return-transition (assoc base\n463\t                              :pc (:pc entry)\n464\t                              :frames (:frames entry)\n465\t                              :continuation (:continuation entry)\n466\t                              :store-of (:store-of entry)\n467\t                              :halted? false)\n468\t                       val)\n469\t    (let [pc (:pc entry)\n470\t          body (body-of-pc (:segment base) pc)\n471\t          reg-count (:registers body)\n472\t          dest (:dest entry)\n473\t          restored-regs\n474\t          (reduce (fn [acc [r v]] (assoc acc r v))\n475\t                  (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n476\t                  (:regs entry))\n477\t          final-regs (if (some? dest)\n478\t                       (assoc restored-regs dest val)\n479\t                       restored-regs)]\n480\t      (assoc base\n481\t             :pc pc\n482\t             :frames (:frames entry)\n483\t             :registers final-regs\n484\t             :continuation (:continuation entry)\n485\t             :store-of (:store-of entry)\n486\t             :value val\n487\t             :halted? false))))\n488\t\n489\t\n490\t(defn register-restore\n491\t  \"The register VM's restore function, `base entry val -> state`\n492\t   (design section 5.2.3). Validates format identity and that the entry's\n493\t   `:image` is a row of the offset table (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3,\n494\t   r6; `:hash` is never a restore key, since it changes at every\n495\t   `attach-image`), checks that the payload is defect-free via\n496\t   effects/continuation-defect, checks that `val` is plain data, handles\n497\t   the FFI two-step, and delivers `val` via `:write-result` or\n498\t   `:return-result`. The entry restores registers only and never assigns\n499\t   `:segment`: the code space is kernel state.\"\n500\t  [base entry val]\n501\t  (check-format! base entry)\n502\t  (when-let [defect (effects/continuation-defect entry)]\n503\t    (throw (ex-info \"Corrupt or tampered continuation payload\"\n504\t                    defect)))\n505\t  (when-not (vm/machine-data? val)\n506\t    (throw (ex-info \"Resume value must be plain data\"\n507\t                    {:rule :resume-value, :val val})))\n508\t  (if (:request-sent entry)\n509\t    (-> base\n510\t        (update :wait-set (fnil conj [])\n511\t                (ffi/response-wait-entry entry (:call-id entry)))\n512\t        (assoc :value :yin/blocked\n513\t               :blocked? true\n514\t               :halted? false))\n515\t    (let [call-id (:call-id entry)\n516\t          base (if call-id (update base :parked dissoc call-id) base)\n517\t          val (if call-id (ffi/call-result val call-id) val)]\n518\t      (write-back base entry val))))\n519\t\n520\t\n521\t;; =============================================================================\n522\t;; Effects & FFI dispatch\n523\t;; =============================================================================\n524\t\n525\t(defn- payload-of\n526\t  \"The continuation payload of `inst` (`effects/continuation-payload`),\n527\t   carrying the running body's module store when there is one.\"\n528\t  [vm inst]\n529\t  (cond-> (effects/continuation-payload vm inst)\n530\t    (:store-of vm) (assoc :store-of (:store-of vm))))\n531\t\n532\t\n533\t(defn- park-entry-fns\n534\t  [payload]\n535\t  {:stream/put (fn [_state effect result]\n536\t                 (assoc payload\n537\t                        :reason :put\n538\t                        :stream-id (:stream-id result)\n539\t                        :datom (:val effect))),\n540\t   :stream/next (fn [_state _effect result]\n541\t                  (assoc payload\n542\t                         :reason :next\n543\t                         :cursor-ref (:cursor-ref result)\n544\t                         :stream-id (:stream-id result))),\n545\t   :module/require (fn [_state _effect _result] payload)})\n546\t\n547\t\n548\t(defn- run-effect\n549\t  [vm effect inst]\n550\t  (let [opts (when (rcode/boundary-opcodes (first inst))\n551\t               {:park-entry-fns\n552\t                (park-entry-fns (payload-of vm inst))})\n553\t        pc' (inc (:pc vm))\n554\t        {:keys [state value blocked?]}\n555\t        (engine/handle-effect vm effect opts)]\n556\t    (if blocked?\n557\t      (assoc state :pc pc')\n558\t      (let [rd (nth inst 1)]\n559\t        (assoc state\n560\t               :pc pc'\n561\t               :registers (assoc (:registers state) rd value))))))\n562\t\n563\t\n564\t(defn- run-call-effect\n565\t  [vm effect inst]\n566\t  (let [payload (payload-of vm inst)\n567\t        tail? (true? (nth inst 4))\n568\t        pc' (inc (:pc vm))\n569\t        {:keys [state value blocked?]}\n570\t        (engine/handle-effect vm\n571\t                              effect\n572\t                              {:park-entry-fns (park-entry-fns payload)})]\n573\t    (if blocked?\n574\t      (assoc state :pc pc')\n575\t      (if tail?\n576\t        (return-transition state value)\n577\t        (let [rd (nth inst 1)]\n578\t          (assoc state\n579\t                 :pc pc'\n580\t                 :registers (assoc (:registers state) rd value)))))))\n581\t\n582\t\n583\t(defn- ffi-call\n584\t  [vm inst]\n585\t  (let [{:keys [pc registers resources]} vm\n586\t        op (nth inst 2)\n587\t        arg-regs (nth inst 3)\n588\t        args (mapv #(nth registers %) arg-regs)\n589\t        {:keys [call-in]} (ffi/require-call-pair! resources op)\n590\t        payload (payload-of vm inst)\n591\t        call-id (ffi/call-id vm (engine/park-id vm))\n592\t        ;; the request carries `args` out of the VM's view\n593\t        parked (engine/park-continuation (assoc (engine/pin-refs vm args)\n594\t                                                :pc (inc pc))\n595\t                                         payload\n596\t                                         call-id)\n597\t        request (apply2/request call-id op args)\n598\t        result (ffi/put-request vm call-in request)\n599\t        blocked (fn [entry]\n600\t                  (-> parked\n601\t                      (update :wait-set (fnil conj []) entry)\n602\t                      (assoc :value :yin/blocked\n603\t                             :blocked? true\n604\t                             :halted? false)))]\n605\t    (case (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n606\t      :dao.stream/ok (blocked (ffi/response-wait-entry payload call-id))\n607\t      :dao.stream/full (blocked (assoc payload\n608\t                                       :request-sent true\n609\t                                       :call-id call-id\n610\t                                       :op op\n611\t                                       :reason :put\n612\t                                       :stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key\n613\t                                       :datom request))\n614\t      (throw (ex-info \"FFI request could not be appended\"\n615\t                      {:op op,\n616\t                       :outcome (or (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n617\t                                    (:dao.stream.apply/outcome result))})))))\n618\t\n619\t\n620\t;; =============================================================================\n621\t;; Instruction step function\n622\t;; =============================================================================\n623\t\n624\t(defn- step1\n625\t  \"Execute exactly one instruction and return the resulting VM.\"\n626\t  [vm]\n627\t  (let [{:keys [segment pc frames free-env registers continuation\n628\t                primitives modules store-of]} vm\n629\t        inst (nth (:instructions segment) pc)\n630\t        op (nth inst 0)]\n631\t    (case op\n632\t      :const\n633\t      (assoc vm\n634\t             :pc (inc pc)\n635\t             :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) (nth inst 2)))\n636\t\n637\t      :load-bound\n638\t      (let [val (frame-value frames (nth inst 2) (nth inst 3))]\n639\t        (assoc vm\n640\t               :pc (inc pc)\n641\t               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n642\t\n643\t      :load-free\n644\t      (let [val (engine/resolve-var free-env\n645\t                                    (engine/active-store vm store-of)\n646\t                                    primitives modules (nth inst 2))]\n647\t        (assoc vm\n648\t               :pc (inc pc)\n649\t               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n650\t\n651\t      :closure\n652\t      (let [clos (values/closure (:owner vm)\n653\t                                 (cond-> {:type :closure,\n654\t                                          :arity (nth inst 2),\n655\t                                          :body-pc (nth inst 3),\n656\t                                          :frames frames}\n657\t                                   store-of (assoc :store-of store-of)))]\n658\t        (assoc vm\n659\t               :pc (inc pc)\n660\t               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) clos)))\n661\t\n662\t      :move\n663\t      (let [val (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n664\t        (assoc vm\n665\t               :pc (inc pc)\n666\t               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n667\t\n668\t      :call\n669\t      (let [rd (nth inst 1)\n670\t            fn-reg (nth inst 2)\n671\t            arg-regs (nth inst 3)\n672\t            tail? (nth inst 4)\n673\t            live (nth inst 5)\n674\t            f (nth registers fn-reg)\n675\t            args (mapv #(nth registers %) arg-regs)]\n676\t        (case (engine/operator-kind vm f)\n677\t          :closure\n678\t          (let [c (values/payload f)\n679\t                callee-pc (:body-pc c)\n680\t                callee-body (body-of-pc segment callee-pc)\n681\t                callee-arity (:arity c)\n682\t                callee-reg-count (:registers callee-body)\n683\t                locals (bind-positional callee-arity args)\n684\t                body-frames (conj (:frames c) locals)\n685\t                callee-regs (into locals\n686\t                                  (repeat (- callee-reg-count callee-arity)\n687\t                                          nil))\n688\t                ;; The frame carries no code space (r7): its absolute\n689\t                ;; :return-pc survives every later append.\n690\t                continuation'\n691\t                (if tail?\n692\t                  continuation\n693\t                  (conj continuation\n694\t                        (cond-> {:site-pc pc,\n695\t                                 :return-pc (inc pc),\n696\t                                 :frames frames,\n697\t                                 :regs (mapv (fn [r] [r (nth registers r)])\n698\t                                             live),\n699\t                                 :live live,\n700\t                                 :dest rd}\n701\t                          store-of (assoc :store-of store-of))))]\n702\t            (assoc vm\n703\t                   :pc callee-pc\n704\t                   :frames body-frames\n705\t                   :registers callee-regs\n706\t                   :continuation continuation'\n707\t                   :store-of (:store-of c)))\n708\t\n709\t          :host-fn\n710\t          (let [result (apply f args)]\n711\t            (if (module/effect? result)\n712\t              (run-call-effect (engine/check-callee-effect! vm f result)\n713\t                               result\n714\t                               inst)\n715\t              (if tail?\n716\t                (return-transition vm result)\n717\t                (assoc vm\n718\t                       :pc (inc pc)\n719\t                       :registers (assoc registers rd result)))))\n720\t\n721\t          ;; A captured continuation: abortive, so the call site's\n722\t          ;; registers, frames and return frames are dropped and the\n723\t          ;; captured ones restored with the argument in the capture's\n724\t          ;; destination register. The store is not a register. An\n725\t          ;; in-machine value, so only its identity is checked: the\n726\t          ;; payload-defect and plain-data gates are for a continuation\n727\t          ;; or value crossing into the machine, and a capture's live\n728\t          ;; registers may hold closures and primitives.\n729\t          :continuation\n730\t          (let [v (engine/continuation-argument args)\n731\t                c (values/payload f)]\n732\t            (check-format! vm c)\n733\t            (write-back vm c v))))\n734\t\n735\t      :branch-false\n736\t      (let [c (nth registers (nth inst 1))]\n737\t        (assoc vm :pc (if c (inc pc) (nth inst 2))))\n738\t\n739\t      :jump\n740\t      (assoc vm :pc (nth inst 1))\n741\t\n742\t      :return\n743\t      (return-transition vm (nth registers (nth inst 1)))\n744\t\n745\t      :halt\n746\t      (assoc vm\n747\t             :halted? true, :value (nth registers (nth inst 1)), :store-of nil)\n748\t\n749\t      ;; A module closure's store instructions route to its module store,\n750\t      ;; with no ambient fallback (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r7).\n751\t      :store-get\n752\t      (assoc vm\n753\t             :pc (inc pc)\n754\t             :registers (assoc registers\n755\t                               (nth inst 1)\n756\t                               (get (engine/active-store vm store-of)\n757\t                                    (nth inst 2))))\n758\t\n759\t      :store-put\n760\t      (let [key (nth inst 2)\n761\t            val (nth inst 3)]\n762\t        (assoc (engine/put-active vm store-of key val)\n763\t               :pc (inc pc)\n764\t               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n765\t\n766\t      ;; :define -- the definition transition: register `rs` is written\n767\t      ;; under the literal name and into `rd`. The operator is never\n768\t      ;; resolved (Rule R).\n769\t      :define\n770\t      (let [val (nth registers (nth inst 3))]\n771\t        (assoc (engine/put-active vm store-of (nth inst 2) val)\n772\t               :pc (inc pc)\n773\t               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n774\t\n775\t      :gensym\n776\t      (let [[id vm'] (engine/gensym vm (nth inst 2))]\n777\t        (assoc vm'\n778\t               :pc (inc pc)\n779\t               :registers (assoc (:registers vm') (nth inst 1) id)))\n780\t\n781\t      :stream-make\n782\t      (let [cap (or (nth inst 2) vm/default-stream-capacity)]\n783\t        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/make {:capacity cap}) inst))\n784\t\n785\t      :stream-put\n786\t      (let [sr (nth registers (nth inst 2))\n787\t            vr (nth registers (nth inst 3))]\n788\t        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/put {:stream sr, :val vr}) inst))\n789\t\n790\t      :stream-cursor\n791\t      (let [sr (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n792\t        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/cursor {:stream sr}) inst))\n793\t\n794\t      :stream-next\n795\t      (let [cr (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n796\t        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/next {:cursor cr}) inst))\n797\t\n798\t      :stream-close\n799\t      (let [sr (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n800\t        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/close {:stream sr}) inst))\n801\t\n802\t      :current-continuation\n803\t      (let [payload (payload-of vm inst)\n804\t            reified (values/continuation\n805\t                      (:owner vm)\n806\t                      (merge {:type :reified-continuation} payload))]\n807\t        (assoc vm\n808\t               :pc (inc pc)\n809\t               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) reified)))\n810\t\n811\t      :park\n812\t      (let [payload (payload-of vm inst)]\n813\t        (engine/park-continuation (assoc vm :pc (inc pc)) payload))\n814\t\n815\t      :resume\n816\t      (let [val (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n817\t        (engine/resume-continuation vm (nth inst 1) val register-restore))\n818\t\n819\t      :ffi-call\n820\t      (ffi-call vm inst)\n821\t\n822\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"Unknown opcode in segment: \" op)\n823\t                      {:rule :unknown-opcode, :op op, :pc pc})))))\n824\t\n825\t\n826\t;; =============================================================================\n827\t;; Scheduling & Protocol Implementations\n828\t;; =============================================================================\n829\t\n830\t(defn- run-scheduler\n831\t  \"The raw runner: already-loaded work only, through the shared scheduler\n832\t   loop with this machine's step function and its restore bound into the\n833\t   engine's run-queue resumption. `ffi/maybe-run` wraps this for bridge\n834\t   dispatch.\"\n835\t  [vm]\n836\t  (engine/run-loop vm\n837\t                   engine/active-continuation?\n838\t                   step1\n839\t                   #(engine/resume-from-run-queue % register-restore)))\n840\t\n841\t\n842\t(extend-type DebruijnRegisterVM\n843\t  vm/IVM\n844\t  (step [this]\n845\t    (cond (engine/active-continuation? this) (step1 this)\n846\t          (or (:blocked? this) (seq (:ready-queue this)))\n847\t          (engine/scheduler-round this register-restore)\n848\t          :else this))\n849\t  (run [this] (ffi/maybe-run this run-scheduler))\n850\t  (eval [_ ast]\n851\t    (throw\n852\t      (ex-info\n853\t        (str \"The de Bruijn register kernel executes raw instruction vectors, \"\n854\t             \"not AST: lower and adapt it first \"\n855\t             \"(yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile/adapt), then load and run the \"\n856\t             \"resulting image\")\n857\t        {:ast ast})))\n858\t  ;; A reset is a fresh run over the held code space, not a load: the\n859\t  ;; offset table is kernel state only the loaders and `attach-image`\n860\t  ;; write (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r7), so it survives.\n861\t  (reset [this]\n862\t    (assoc (install-image this (:segment this)) :images (:images this)))\n863\t  (halted? [this] (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? this))\n864\t  (blocked? [this] (engine/vm-blocked? this))\n865\t  (value [this] (engine/vm-value this))\n866\t\n867\t  vm/IVMState\n868\t  (control [this] {:pc (:pc this)})\n869\t  (environment [_this]\n870\t    (throw\n871\t      (ex-info\n872\t        (str \"environment is not implemented: the design defers it until a \"\n873\t             \"frame-to-named lift exists\")\n874\t        {:rule :not-yet-supported})))\n875\t  (store [this] (:store this))\n876\t  (continuation [this] (:continuation this)))\n877\t\n878\t\n879\t;; =============================================================================\n880\t;; Module kernel (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3)\n881\t;; =============================================================================\n882\t;; As the stack kernel: a positional closure lifts by the offset table row\n883\t;; holding its body pc and lowers by the receiving table's row.\n884\t\n885\t(defn- binding-mismatch!\n886\t  [marker]\n887\t  (throw (ex-info \"Closure marker of another binding discipline or format\"\n888\t                  {:reason :binding-mismatch,\n889\t                   :binding (:yin.k/binding marker),\n890\t                   :format (:yin.k/format marker),\n891\t                   :expected-format format-tag})))\n892\t\n893\t\n894\t(extend-type DebruijnRegisterVM\n895\t  module/IModuleKernel\n896\t  (link-format [_] {:format format-tag, :contract vm/register-contract})\n897\t  (spawn-module\n898\t    [vm image {:keys [modules origin ancestry capability-secret]}]\n899\t    (create-vm image\n900\t               {:free-env (:free-env vm),\n901\t                :primitives (:primitives vm),\n902\t                :modules modules,\n903\t                :make-stream (:make-stream vm),\n904\t                :link-request (get (:resources vm)\n905\t                                   module/link-request-resource),\n906\t                :link-response (get (:resources vm)\n907\t                                    module/link-response-resource),\n908\t                :origin origin,\n909\t                :ancestry ancestry,\n910\t                :capability-secret capability-secret,\n911\t                :secret-source (:secret-source vm),\n912\t                :attach-stream (:attach-stream vm),\n913\t                :gc-threshold (:base (:gc vm)),\n914\t                :contract vm/register-contract}))\n915\t  (image-identity [_ image] (rcode/register-hash image))\n916\t  (image-holds? [_ image segment] (= segment (rcode/register-hash image)))\n917\t  (attach-module [vm image] (attach-image vm image vm/register-contract))\n918\t  (lift-closure [vm closure encode]\n919\t    (let [[ident rel] (or (image-pc vm (:body-pc closure))\n920\t                          (throw (ex-info \"Closure body in no held image\"\n921\t                                          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable,\n922\t                                           :yin.k/kind :unrooted-body})))]\n923\t      (cond-> {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/closure,\n924\t               :yin.k/binding :positional,\n925\t               :yin.k/format format-tag,\n926\t               :yin.k/segment ident,\n927\t               :yin.k/entry rel,\n928\t               :yin.k/arity (:arity closure),\n929\t               :yin.k/frames (mapv #(mapv encode %) (:frames closure))}\n930\t        (:store-of closure) (assoc :yin.k/store-of (:store-of closure)))))\n931\t  (lower-closure [vm marker decode]\n932\t    (when-not (and (= :positional (:yin.k/binding marker))\n933\t                   (= format-tag (:yin.k/format marker)))\n934\t      (binding-mismatch! marker))\n935\t    (let [pc (absolute-pc vm [(:yin.k/segment marker) (:yin.k/entry marker)])]\n936\t      (when (nil? pc)\n937\t        (throw (ex-info \"Closure origin image is not attached\"\n938\t                        {:reason :origin-not-attached,\n939\t                         :segment (:yin.k/segment marker)})))\n940\t      ;; the arity is that of a `:closure` of the attached code whose body\n941\t      ;; this is, never the wire's\n942\t      (when-not (some #(and (= :closure (nth % 0))\n943\t                            (= (:yin.k/arity marker) (nth % 2))\n944\t                            (= pc (nth % 3)))\n945\t                      (:instructions (:segment vm)))\n946\t        (engine/marker-mismatch! marker))\n947\t      (values/closure\n948\t        (:owner vm)\n949\t        (cond-> {:type :closure,\n950\t                 :arity (:yin.k/arity marker),\n951\t                 :body-pc pc,\n952\t                 :frames (mapv #(mapv decode %) (:yin.k/frames marker))}\n953\t          (:yin.k/store-of marker)\n954\t          (assoc :store-of (:yin.k/store-of marker))))))\n955\t  (gc-roots [vm]\n956\t    {:kernel [(:continuation vm)],\n957\t     :values [(:frames vm) (:registers vm) (:value vm)]})\n958\t  ;; A register payload (a wait, ready or parked entry, or a reified\n959\t  ;; continuation) names the code space as `:segment`; that is code, so\n960\t  ;; every other key is traced. Closures and return frames hold no code.\n961\t  (gc-children [_ x]\n962\t    (when (and (map? x) (= format-tag (:format x)))\n963\t      {:values (into [] (vals (dissoc x :segment)))})))\n964\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b921a1a6-65e4-4bc4-853c-fc87c8b912fe","uuid":"d04530c4-5a5c-4e7c-852e-329f36653e90","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:42:32.360Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.debruijn.register\n  \"R4 (docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md S5, S6 R4): the register\n   execution kernel that interprets positional register images\n   `{:bodies [...], :instructions [...]}` under contract version 4\n   (the \\\"r2\\\" contract).\n\n   The register kernel is a sibling to `yin.vm.debruijn.stack` (B3/B4) and\n   `yin.vm.semantic`. It preserves B3's frame direction, closure capture,\n   nil-fill and extra-argument rules, and B0 normalization. It executes\n   only validator-approved images.\n\n   State: `{:segment :hash :images :pc :frames :free-env :registers\n            :continuation :store :blocked? :halted? :wait-set :ready-queue\n            :parked :id-counter :value :make-stream :bridge :primitives\n            :modules}`.\n\n   Continuation transport: register continuations and stack continuations\n   are not interchangeable (section 5.1). Payloads carry `:format\n   :yin.debruijn.register`, `:hash R` of the code space at the time, and\n   `:image`, the offset-table row their pc falls in (yin.vm.linker.md\n   section 7.3, r6). A foreign format or an `:image` the table does not\n   hold is refused with qualified `:continuation-format` diagnostics.\n   Resume values must be plain data, refusing host exceptions with\n   `:resume-value`.\n\n   The kernel implements all 23 opcodes, Rule R's `:define` included,\n   across the pure-program tier and the\n   effects tier, connecting to `yin.vm.engine` via `register-restore` and\n   per-site wait-entry builders.\"\n  (:require [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-effects :as effects]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; State\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defrecord DebruijnRegisterVM\n  [segment      ; {:bodies [...], :instructions [...]}\n   hash         ; R of segment (yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash)\n   images       ; offset table: [[identity offset length] ...], base first\n   pc           ; program counter into :instructions\n   frames       ; positional lexical frame stack, outermost first\n   free-env     ; initial free-name environment map\n   registers    ; persistent vector for current body's register file\n   continuation ; vector of return frames (innermost last)\n   store        ; heap map\n   blocked?     ; engine: boolean\n   halted?      ; engine: boolean\n   wait-set     ; engine: vector of wait entries\n   ready-queue  ; engine: vector of woken entries\n   parked       ; engine: map of parked continuations\n   id-counter   ; engine: counter for gensym, stream, and park ids\n   value        ; engine: last computed value\n   make-stream  ; host stream constructor or nil\n   bridge       ; host FFI bridge or nil\n   primitives   ; primitive registry for :load-free\n   modules      ; module registry for :load-free and effect dispatch\n   store-of     ; the running body's module store address, or nil\n   resources    ; private engine resources: the link pair\n   origin       ; this task's origin tag for link ids\n   ancestry     ; the modules installing on this task's install chain\n   gc])         ; {:since :base :threshold :pinned}: heap reclamation\n\n\n(def format-tag\n  \"The model tag every register payload carries as `:format`.\"\n  effects/format-tag)\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Body & frame addressing\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- body-of-pc\n  \"Return the declared body map covering instruction `pc` in `segment`.\"\n  [{:keys [bodies]} pc]\n  (some (fn [{:keys [start end] :as body}]\n          (when (and (<= start pc) (<= pc end)) body))\n        bodies))\n\n\n(defn- frame-value\n  \"Frame 0 for `:load-bound` is the INNERMOST frame, read from the END of\n   `:frames`. `frames` is outermost-first, so depth `d` is\n   `(count frames) - 1 - d`.\"\n  [frames depth position]\n  (let [n (count frames)\n        idx (- n 1 depth)]\n    (when (or (neg? idx) (>= idx n))\n      (throw (ex-info \"load-bound: depth out of range\"\n                      {:rule :load-bound-depth, :depth depth,\n                       :frame-count n})))\n    (let [frame (nth frames idx)]\n      (when (or (neg? position) (>= position (count frame)))\n        (throw (ex-info \"load-bound: position out of range\"\n                        {:rule :load-bound-position, :depth depth,\n                         :position position, :frame-arity (count frame)})))\n      (nth frame position))))\n\n\n(defn- bind-positional\n  \"Positional parameter binding: missing arguments are nil-filled,\n   extra arguments dropped.\"\n  [arity args]\n  (vec (take arity (concat args (repeat nil)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Image loading & VM construction\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- empty-segment?\n  [segment]\n  (or (nil? segment)\n      (empty? segment)\n      (and (map? segment) (empty? (:instructions segment)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private empty-image {:bodies [], :instructions []})\n\n\n(defn- install-image\n  \"Install `segment` as the one image. A non-empty image must pass the\n   register validator. The offset table restarts at the base row\n   `[R 0 n]`.\"\n  [vm segment]\n  (let [empty-seg? (empty-segment? segment)]\n    (if empty-seg?\n      (assoc vm\n             :segment empty-image\n             :hash nil\n             :images [[(rcode/register-hash empty-image) 0 0]]\n             :pc 0\n             :frames []\n             :registers []\n             :continuation []\n             :halted? true\n             :blocked? false\n             :value nil)\n      (if-let [defect (rcode/register-image-defect segment)]\n        (throw (ex-info (str \"Invalid register image: \" (:rule defect))\n                        defect))\n        (let [body0 (first (:bodies segment))\n              reg-count (or (:registers body0) 0)\n              r (rcode/register-hash segment)]\n          (assoc vm\n                 :segment segment\n                 :hash r\n                 :images [[r 0 (count (:instructions segment))]]\n                 :pc 0\n                 :frames []\n                 :registers (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n                 :continuation []\n                 :halted? false\n                 :blocked? false\n                 :value nil))))))\n\n\n(defn load-image\n  \"Load `segment` (a register image `{:bodies [...], :instructions [...]}`)\n   into `vm` as its one image: R is computed, the registers are reset to\n   pc 0 with empty frames and continuation, and the machine is running\n   unless the segment is empty. The offset table restarts at `[R 0 n]`, so\n   a continuation parked under an earlier image names no row of it and\n   `register-restore` refuses it.\n\n   `contract` is required and compared with `vm/register-contract` first\n   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`); a non-empty image must then\n   pass the register validator, Rule R included. An empty segment admits\n   no code and needs neither.\"\n  [vm segment contract]\n  (when-not (empty-segment? segment)\n    (vm/check-contract! vm/register-contract contract))\n  (install-image vm segment))\n\n\n(defn relocate\n  \"Shift every `:pc`-kind operand of `inst` by `offset`.\"\n  [offset inst]\n  (reduce (fn [inst [i [_ kind]]]\n            (if (= :pc kind) (update inst (inc i) + offset) inst))\n          inst\n          (map-indexed vector (get rcode/opcode-table (nth inst 0)))))\n\n\n(defn attach-image\n  \"Extend the code space of `vm` with `image`, non-destructively\n   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, act 3): `image` is admitted alone as\n   `load-image` admits it, relocated by the held instruction count, and\n   appended, `:bodies` shifted likewise; one `[identity offset length]`\n   row, identity R of `image`, is appended to the offset table; `:hash`\n   becomes R of the concatenation. `:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`,\n   `:continuation`, and every other register are unchanged: appending\n   moves no instruction already held. An image whose identity is already\n   a row is not attached twice, and an empty image, which adds no code,\n   is not attached at all.\"\n  [vm image contract]\n  (when-not (empty-segment? image)\n    (vm/check-contract! vm/register-contract contract)\n    (when-let [defect (rcode/register-image-defect image)]\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"Invalid register image: \" (:rule defect))\n                      defect))))\n  (let [ident (when-not (empty-segment? image) (rcode/register-hash image))]\n    (if (or (nil? ident) (some #(= ident (nth % 0)) (:images vm)))\n      vm\n      (let [held (:segment vm)\n            offset (count (:instructions held))\n            shift-body #(-> % (update :start + offset) (update :end + offset))\n            combined {:bodies (into (:bodies held)\n                                    (map shift-body)\n                                    (:bodies image)),\n                      :instructions (into (:instructions held)\n                                          (map #(relocate offset %))\n                                          (:instructions image))}]\n        (assoc vm\n               :segment combined\n               :hash (rcode/register-hash combined)\n               :images (conj (:images vm)\n                             [ident offset\n                              (count (:instructions image))]))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Layouts: the ordered image list a code space is built from (UCF v2, 4.1)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def max-layout-length\n  \"2^52-1: the largest instruction-count sum a layout may name.\"\n  4503599627370495)\n\n\n(defn layout\n  \"The ordered identities of `vm`'s offset table: its current layout.\"\n  [vm]\n  (mapv #(nth % 0) (:images vm)))\n\n\n(defn compose\n  \"The code space `images`, the component register images in layout\n   order, build: `{:segment :hash :images}` where `:segment` is the\n   relocated concatenation (bodies shifted likewise), `:images` the\n   offset table derived by prefix sums, and `:hash` its R -- nil while\n   no instruction is held, the empty base's convention.  A length sum\n   beyond 2^52-1 refuses with `:layout-overflow`; nothing here validates\n   an image.\"\n  [images]\n  (let [{:keys [bodies instructions rows]}\n        (reduce (fn [{:keys [bodies instructions rows]} image]\n                  (let [offset (count instructions)\n                        n (count (:instructions image))]\n                    (when (> (+ offset n) max-layout-length)\n                      (throw (ex-info \"Layout length overflow\"\n                                      {:rule :layout-overflow})))\n                    {:bodies (into bodies\n                                   (map #(-> %\n                                             (update :start + offset)\n                                             (update :end + offset)))\n                                   (:bodies image))\n                     :instructions (into instructions\n                                         (map #(relocate offset %))\n                                         (:instructions image))\n                     :rows (conj rows [(rcode/register-hash image) offset n])}))\n                {:bodies [] :instructions [] :rows []}\n                images)\n        segment {:bodies bodies :instructions instructions}]\n    {:segment segment\n     :hash (when (seq instructions) (rcode/register-hash segment))\n     :images rows}))\n\n\n(defn layout-images\n  \"The component image of each row of the offset table `images` over\n   `segment`, relocated back to its own pc 0, in table order; nil\n   unless the table covers the segment exactly and every slice rehashes\n   to its row's identity.\"\n  [segment images]\n  (when (and (map? segment) (nil? (effects/table-defect\n                                    (count (:instructions segment)) images)))\n    (let [slices (mapv #(effects/image-slice segment %) images)]\n      (when (every? true?\n                    (map (fn [[ident _ _] slice]\n                           (= ident (rcode/register-hash slice)))\n                         images slices))\n        slices))))\n\n\n(defn rebuild\n  \"`vm` over the code space `images` (the component images in layout\n   order) build, each non-empty one admitted alone under the register\n   contract; the registers are reset.  The store, the parked map, the\n   queues and the composition values survive.\"\n  [vm images]\n  (doseq [image images\n          :when (not (empty-segment? image))]\n    (when-let [defect (rcode/register-image-defect image)]\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"Invalid register image: \" (:rule defect))\n                      defect))))\n  (let [{:keys [segment hash images]} (compose images)\n        body0 (first (:bodies segment))]\n    (assoc vm\n           :segment segment\n           :hash hash\n           :images images\n           :pc 0\n           :frames []\n           :registers (vec (repeat (or (:registers body0) 0) nil))\n           :continuation []\n           :store-of nil)))\n\n\n(defn image-pc\n  \"Lift an absolute `pc` of `vm` to `[identity rel-pc]` by its offset\n   table, or nil when no row holds it.\"\n  [vm pc]\n  (when-let [[ident off] (effects/image-row (:images vm) pc)]\n    [ident (- pc off)]))\n\n\n(defn absolute-pc\n  \"Lower `[identity rel-pc]` to an absolute pc of `vm` by its offset\n   table, or nil when the identity is no row of it or `rel-pc` is no pc\n   `image-pc` lifts into that row.\"\n  [vm [ident rel-pc]]\n  (let [images (:images vm)]\n    (some (fn [[id off :as row]]\n            (when (and (= id ident)\n                       (nat-int? rel-pc)\n                       (= row (effects/image-row images (+ off rel-pc))))\n              (+ off rel-pc)))\n          images)))\n\n\n(defn create-vm\n  \"Build a fresh `DebruijnRegisterVM` over `segment`.\n   Options: `:free-env`, `:store`, `:primitives`, `:modules`, `:make-stream`,\n   `:call-in`/`:call-out`/`:call-out-cursor`/`:ffi-caller-id`/\n   `:call-capacity`, `:bridge`, and `:contract`, the\n   segment's stamp, required when `segment` is non-empty (`load-image`). A\n   `:free-env`, `:store`, or `:primitives` binding a reserved name is\n   refused (Rule R). `:link-request`/`:link-response` (the link pair\n   `require` lowers to), `:origin`, and `:ancestry` are\n   `yin.vm/empty-state`'s.\"\n  ([segment] (create-vm segment {}))\n  ([segment opts]\n   (let [base (vm/empty-state\n                (assoc (select-keys opts [:modules :make-stream :call-in\n                                          :call-out :call-out-cursor\n                                          :ffi-caller-id :call-capacity\n                                          :link-request :link-response\n                                          :origin :ancestry\n                                          :capability-secret :secret-source\n                                          :attach-stream :gc-threshold])\n                       :primitives (or (:primitives opts) {})))]\n     (-> (map->DebruijnRegisterVM\n           {:segment {:bodies [], :instructions []},\n            :store-of nil,\n            :resources (:resources base),\n            :origin (:origin base),\n            :ancestry (:ancestry base),\n            :capability-secret (:capability-secret base),\n            :owner (:owner base),\n            :secret-source (:secret-source base),\n            :attach-stream (:attach-stream base),\n            :hash nil,\n            :images [],\n            :pc 0,\n            :frames [],\n            :free-env (vm/check-bindings! :env (or (:free-env opts) {})),\n            :registers [],\n            :continuation [],\n            :store (merge (:store base)\n                          (vm/check-bindings! :store (:store opts))),\n            :blocked? false,\n            :halted? true,\n            :wait-set [],\n            :ready-queue [],\n            :parked {},\n            :heap (:heap base),\n            :gc (:gc base),\n            :id-counter 0,\n            :ffi-caller-id (:ffi-caller-id base),\n            :value nil,\n            :make-stream (:make-stream base),\n            :bridge nil,\n            :primitives (:primitives base),\n            :callable-effects (:callable-effects base),\n            :modules (or (:modules opts) {})})\n         (load-image segment (:contract opts))\n         (ffi/attach (:bridge opts))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Return transitions & restore\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- return-transition\n  \"Unified return transition: restores caller frame from continuation if\n   pending, otherwise halts the VM with `val`. Only pc, frames, registers,\n   and continuation are restored (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r7): a\n   frame carries no code space, so an image attached while the call was\n   in flight stays attached, and the absolute `:return-pc` still names\n   the caller's instruction in the grown code space.\"\n  [vm val]\n  (let [continuation (:continuation vm)]\n    (if (seq continuation)\n      (let [frame (peek continuation)\n            return-pc (:return-pc frame)\n            body (body-of-pc (:segment vm) return-pc)\n            reg-count (:registers body)\n            dest (:dest frame)\n            restored-regs (reduce (fn [acc [r v]] (assoc acc r v))\n                                  (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n                                  (:regs frame))\n            final-regs (if (some? dest)\n                         (assoc restored-regs dest val)\n                         restored-regs)]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc return-pc\n               :frames (:frames frame)\n               :registers final-regs\n               :continuation (pop continuation)\n               :store-of (:store-of frame)\n               :value val\n               :halted? false))\n      (assoc vm :halted? true, :value val, :store-of nil))))\n\n\n(defn- refuse-continuation!\n  [base entry]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Cannot restore a continuation of another model or image\"\n                  {:reason :foreign-format,\n                   :rule :continuation-format,\n                   :format (:format entry),\n                   :hash (:hash entry),\n                   :image (:image entry),\n                   :expected-format format-tag,\n                   :expected-hash (:hash base),\n                   :images (:images base)})))\n\n\n(defn- check-format!\n  \"Refuse `entry` unless it is this model's payload for a row of the offset\n   table (r6).\"\n  [base entry]\n  (when-not (and (= format-tag (:format entry))\n                 (some #(= (:image entry) (nth % 0)) (:images base)))\n    (refuse-continuation! base entry)))\n\n\n(defn- write-back\n  \"Write `entry`'s registers back and deliver `val` via `:write-result` or\n   `:return-result`. Registers only: `:segment` is kernel state.\"\n  [base entry val]\n  (if (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\n    (return-transition (assoc base\n                              :pc (:pc entry)\n                              :frames (:frames entry)\n                              :continuation (:continuation entry)\n                              :store-of (:store-of entry)\n                              :halted? false)\n                       val)\n    (let [pc (:pc entry)\n          body (body-of-pc (:segment base) pc)\n          reg-count (:registers body)\n          dest (:dest entry)\n          restored-regs\n          (reduce (fn [acc [r v]] (assoc acc r v))\n                  (vec (repeat reg-count nil))\n                  (:regs entry))\n          final-regs (if (some? dest)\n                       (assoc restored-regs dest val)\n                       restored-regs)]\n      (assoc base\n             :pc pc\n             :frames (:frames entry)\n             :registers final-regs\n             :continuation (:continuation entry)\n             :store-of (:store-of entry)\n             :value val\n             :halted? false))))\n\n\n(defn register-restore\n  \"The register VM's restore function, `base entry val -> state`\n   (design section 5.2.3). Validates format identity and that the entry's\n   `:image` is a row of the offset table (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3,\n   r6; `:hash` is never a restore key, since it changes at every\n   `attach-image`), checks that the payload is defect-free via\n   effects/continuation-defect, checks that `val` is plain data, handles\n   the FFI two-step, and delivers `val` via `:write-result` or\n   `:return-result`. The entry restores registers only and never assigns\n   `:segment`: the code space is kernel state.\"\n  [base entry val]\n  (check-format! base entry)\n  (when-let [defect (effects/continuation-defect entry)]\n    (throw (ex-info \"Corrupt or tampered continuation payload\"\n                    defect)))\n  (when-not (vm/machine-data? val)\n    (throw (ex-info \"Resume value must be plain data\"\n                    {:rule :resume-value, :val val})))\n  (if (:request-sent entry)\n    (-> base\n        (update :wait-set (fnil conj [])\n                (ffi/response-wait-entry entry (:call-id entry)))\n        (assoc :value :yin/blocked\n               :blocked? true\n               :halted? false))\n    (let [call-id (:call-id entry)\n          base (if call-id (update base :parked dissoc call-id) base)\n          val (if call-id (ffi/call-result val call-id) val)]\n      (write-back base entry val))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Effects & FFI dispatch\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- payload-of\n  \"The continuation payload of `inst` (`effects/continuation-payload`),\n   carrying the running body's module store when there is one.\"\n  [vm inst]\n  (cond-> (effects/continuation-payload vm inst)\n    (:store-of vm) (assoc :store-of (:store-of vm))))\n\n\n(defn- park-entry-fns\n  [payload]\n  {:stream/put (fn [_state effect result]\n                 (assoc payload\n                        :reason :put\n                        :stream-id (:stream-id result)\n                        :datom (:val effect))),\n   :stream/next (fn [_state _effect result]\n                  (assoc payload\n                         :reason :next\n                         :cursor-ref (:cursor-ref result)\n                         :stream-id (:stream-id result))),\n   :module/require (fn [_state _effect _result] payload)})\n\n\n(defn- run-effect\n  [vm effect inst]\n  (let [opts (when (rcode/boundary-opcodes (first inst))\n               {:park-entry-fns\n                (park-entry-fns (payload-of vm inst))})\n        pc' (inc (:pc vm))\n        {:keys [state value blocked?]}\n        (engine/handle-effect vm effect opts)]\n    (if blocked?\n      (assoc state :pc pc')\n      (let [rd (nth inst 1)]\n        (assoc state\n               :pc pc'\n               :registers (assoc (:registers state) rd value))))))\n\n\n(defn- run-call-effect\n  [vm effect inst]\n  (let [payload (payload-of vm inst)\n        tail? (true? (nth inst 4))\n        pc' (inc (:pc vm))\n        {:keys [state value blocked?]}\n        (engine/handle-effect vm\n                              effect\n                              {:park-entry-fns (park-entry-fns payload)})]\n    (if blocked?\n      (assoc state :pc pc')\n      (if tail?\n        (return-transition state value)\n        (let [rd (nth inst 1)]\n          (assoc state\n                 :pc pc'\n                 :registers (assoc (:registers state) rd value)))))))\n\n\n(defn- ffi-call\n  [vm inst]\n  (let [{:keys [pc registers resources]} vm\n        op (nth inst 2)\n        arg-regs (nth inst 3)\n        args (mapv #(nth registers %) arg-regs)\n        {:keys [call-in]} (ffi/require-call-pair! resources op)\n        payload (payload-of vm inst)\n        call-id (ffi/call-id vm (engine/park-id vm))\n        ;; the request carries `args` out of the VM's view\n        parked (engine/park-continuation (assoc (engine/pin-refs vm args)\n                                                :pc (inc pc))\n                                         payload\n                                         call-id)\n        request (apply2/request call-id op args)\n        result (ffi/put-request vm call-in request)\n        blocked (fn [entry]\n                  (-> parked\n                      (update :wait-set (fnil conj []) entry)\n                      (assoc :value :yin/blocked\n                             :blocked? true\n                             :halted? false)))]\n    (case (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n      :dao.stream/ok (blocked (ffi/response-wait-entry payload call-id))\n      :dao.stream/full (blocked (assoc payload\n                                       :request-sent true\n                                       :call-id call-id\n                                       :op op\n                                       :reason :put\n                                       :stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key\n                                       :datom request))\n      (throw (ex-info \"FFI request could not be appended\"\n                      {:op op,\n                       :outcome (or (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n                                    (:dao.stream.apply/outcome result))})))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Instruction step function\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- step1\n  \"Execute exactly one instruction and return the resulting VM.\"\n  [vm]\n  (let [{:keys [segment pc frames free-env registers continuation\n                primitives modules store-of]} vm\n        inst (nth (:instructions segment) pc)\n        op (nth inst 0)]\n    (case op\n      :const\n      (assoc vm\n             :pc (inc pc)\n             :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) (nth inst 2)))\n\n      :load-bound\n      (let [val (frame-value frames (nth inst 2) (nth inst 3))]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n\n      :load-free\n      (let [val (engine/resolve-var free-env\n                                    (engine/active-store vm store-of)\n                                    primitives modules (nth inst 2))]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n\n      :closure\n      (let [clos (values/closure (:owner vm)\n                                 (cond-> {:type :closure,\n                                          :arity (nth inst 2),\n                                          :body-pc (nth inst 3),\n                                          :frames frames}\n                                   store-of (assoc :store-of store-of)))]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) clos)))\n\n      :move\n      (let [val (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n\n      :call\n      (let [rd (nth inst 1)\n            fn-reg (nth inst 2)\n            arg-regs (nth inst 3)\n            tail? (nth inst 4)\n            live (nth inst 5)\n            f (nth registers fn-reg)\n            args (mapv #(nth registers %) arg-regs)]\n        (case (engine/operator-kind vm f)\n          :closure\n          (let [c (values/payload f)\n                callee-pc (:body-pc c)\n                callee-body (body-of-pc segment callee-pc)\n                callee-arity (:arity c)\n                callee-reg-count (:registers callee-body)\n                locals (bind-positional callee-arity args)\n                body-frames (conj (:frames c) locals)\n                callee-regs (into locals\n                                  (repeat (- callee-reg-count callee-arity)\n                                          nil))\n                ;; The frame carries no code space (r7): its absolute\n                ;; :return-pc survives every later append.\n                continuation'\n                (if tail?\n                  continuation\n                  (conj continuation\n                        (cond-> {:site-pc pc,\n                                 :return-pc (inc pc),\n                                 :frames frames,\n                                 :regs (mapv (fn [r] [r (nth registers r)])\n                                             live),\n                                 :live live,\n                                 :dest rd}\n                          store-of (assoc :store-of store-of))))]\n            (assoc vm\n                   :pc callee-pc\n                   :frames body-frames\n                   :registers callee-regs\n                   :continuation continuation'\n                   :store-of (:store-of c)))\n\n          :host-fn\n          (let [result (apply f args)]\n            (if (module/effect? result)\n              (run-call-effect (engine/check-callee-effect! vm f result)\n                               result\n                               inst)\n              (if tail?\n                (return-transition vm result)\n                (assoc vm\n                       :pc (inc pc)\n                       :registers (assoc registers rd result)))))\n\n          ;; A captured continuation: abortive, so the call site's\n          ;; registers, frames and return frames are dropped and the\n          ;; captured ones restored with the argument in the capture's\n          ;; destination register. The store is not a register. An\n          ;; in-machine value, so only its identity is checked: the\n          ;; payload-defect and plain-data gates are for a continuation\n          ;; or value crossing into the machine, and a capture's live\n          ;; registers may hold closures and primitives.\n          :continuation\n          (let [v (engine/continuation-argument args)\n                c (values/payload f)]\n            (check-format! vm c)\n            (write-back vm c v))))\n\n      :branch-false\n      (let [c (nth registers (nth inst 1))]\n        (assoc vm :pc (if c (inc pc) (nth inst 2))))\n\n      :jump\n      (assoc vm :pc (nth inst 1))\n\n      :return\n      (return-transition vm (nth registers (nth inst 1)))\n\n      :halt\n      (assoc vm\n             :halted? true, :value (nth registers (nth inst 1)), :store-of nil)\n\n      ;; A module closure's store instructions route to its module store,\n      ;; with no ambient fallback (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r7).\n      :store-get\n      (assoc vm\n             :pc (inc pc)\n             :registers (assoc registers\n                               (nth inst 1)\n                               (get (engine/active-store vm store-of)\n                                    (nth inst 2))))\n\n      :store-put\n      (let [key (nth inst 2)\n            val (nth inst 3)]\n        (assoc (engine/put-active vm store-of key val)\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n\n      ;; :define -- the definition transition: register `rs` is written\n      ;; under the literal name and into `rd`. The operator is never\n      ;; resolved (Rule R).\n      :define\n      (let [val (nth registers (nth inst 3))]\n        (assoc (engine/put-active vm store-of (nth inst 2) val)\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) val)))\n\n      :gensym\n      (let [[id vm'] (engine/gensym vm (nth inst 2))]\n        (assoc vm'\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :registers (assoc (:registers vm') (nth inst 1) id)))\n\n      :stream-make\n      (let [cap (or (nth inst 2) vm/default-stream-capacity)]\n        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/make {:capacity cap}) inst))\n\n      :stream-put\n      (let [sr (nth registers (nth inst 2))\n            vr (nth registers (nth inst 3))]\n        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/put {:stream sr, :val vr}) inst))\n\n      :stream-cursor\n      (let [sr (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/cursor {:stream sr}) inst))\n\n      :stream-next\n      (let [cr (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/next {:cursor cr}) inst))\n\n      :stream-close\n      (let [sr (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n        (run-effect vm (module/make-effect :stream/close {:stream sr}) inst))\n\n      :current-continuation\n      (let [payload (payload-of vm inst)\n            reified (values/continuation\n                      (:owner vm)\n                      (merge {:type :reified-continuation} payload))]\n        (assoc vm\n               :pc (inc pc)\n               :registers (assoc registers (nth inst 1) reified)))\n\n      :park\n      (let [payload (payload-of vm inst)]\n        (engine/park-continuation (assoc vm :pc (inc pc)) payload))\n\n      :resume\n      (let [val (nth registers (nth inst 2))]\n        (engine/resume-continuation vm (nth inst 1) val register-restore))\n\n      :ffi-call\n      (ffi-call vm inst)\n\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"Unknown opcode in segment: \" op)\n                      {:rule :unknown-opcode, :op op, :pc pc})))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Scheduling & Protocol Implementations\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- run-scheduler\n  \"The raw runner: already-loaded work only, through the shared scheduler\n   loop with this machine's step function and its restore bound into the\n   engine's run-queue resumption. `ffi/maybe-run` wraps this for bridge\n   dispatch.\"\n  [vm]\n  (engine/run-loop vm\n                   engine/active-continuation?\n                   step1\n                   #(engine/resume-from-run-queue % register-restore)))\n\n\n(extend-type DebruijnRegisterVM\n  vm/IVM\n  (step [this]\n    (cond (engine/active-continuation? this) (step1 this)\n          (or (:blocked? this) (seq (:ready-queue this)))\n          (engine/scheduler-round this register-restore)\n          :else this))\n  (run [this] (ffi/maybe-run this run-scheduler))\n  (eval [_ ast]\n    (throw\n      (ex-info\n        (str \"The de Bruijn register kernel executes raw instruction vectors, \"\n             \"not AST: lower and adapt it first \"\n             \"(yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile/adapt), then load and run the \"\n             \"resulting image\")\n        {:ast ast})))\n  ;; A reset is a fresh run over the held code space, not a load: the\n  ;; offset table is kernel state only the loaders and `attach-image`\n  ;; write (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r7), so it survives.\n  (reset [this]\n    (assoc (install-image this (:segment this)) :images (:images this)))\n  (halted? [this] (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? this))\n  (blocked? [this] (engine/vm-blocked? this))\n  (value [this] (engine/vm-value this))\n\n  vm/IVMState\n  (control [this] {:pc (:pc this)})\n  (environment [_this]\n    (throw\n      (ex-info\n        (str \"environment is not implemented: the design defers it until a \"\n             \"frame-to-named lift exists\")\n        {:rule :not-yet-supported})))\n  (store [this] (:store this))\n  (continuation [this] (:continuation this)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Module kernel (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3)\n;; =============================================================================\n;; As the stack kernel: a positional closure lifts by the offset table row\n;; holding its body pc and lowers by the receiving table's row.\n\n(defn- binding-mismatch!\n  [marker]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Closure marker of another binding discipline or format\"\n                  {:reason :binding-mismatch,\n                   :binding (:yin.k/binding marker),\n                   :format (:yin.k/format marker),\n                   :expected-format format-tag})))\n\n\n(extend-type DebruijnRegisterVM\n  module/IModuleKernel\n  (link-format [_] {:format format-tag, :contract vm/register-contract})\n  (spawn-module\n    [vm image {:keys [modules origin ancestry capability-secret]}]\n    (create-vm image\n               {:free-env (:free-env vm),\n                :primitives (:primitives vm),\n                :modules modules,\n                :make-stream (:make-stream vm),\n                :link-request (get (:resources vm)\n                                   module/link-request-resource),\n                :link-response (get (:resources vm)\n                                    module/link-response-resource),\n                :origin origin,\n                :ancestry ancestry,\n                :capability-secret capability-secret,\n                :secret-source (:secret-source vm),\n                :attach-stream (:attach-stream vm),\n                :gc-threshold (:base (:gc vm)),\n                :contract vm/register-contract}))\n  (image-identity [_ image] (rcode/register-hash image))\n  (image-holds? [_ image segment] (= segment (rcode/register-hash image)))\n  (attach-module [vm image] (attach-image vm image vm/register-contract))\n  (lift-closure [vm closure encode]\n    (let [[ident rel] (or (image-pc vm (:body-pc closure))\n                          (throw (ex-info \"Closure body in no held image\"\n                                          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable,\n                                           :yin.k/kind :unrooted-body})))]\n      (cond-> {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/closure,\n               :yin.k/binding :positional,\n               :yin.k/format format-tag,\n               :yin.k/segment ident,\n               :yin.k/entry rel,\n               :yin.k/arity (:arity closure),\n               :yin.k/frames (mapv #(mapv encode %) (:frames closure))}\n        (:store-of closure) (assoc :yin.k/store-of (:store-of closure)))))\n  (lower-closure [vm marker decode]\n    (when-not (and (= :positional (:yin.k/binding marker))\n                   (= format-tag (:yin.k/format marker)))\n      (binding-mismatch! marker))\n    (let [pc (absolute-pc vm [(:yin.k/segment marker) (:yin.k/entry marker)])]\n      (when (nil? pc)\n        (throw (ex-info \"Closure origin image is not attached\"\n                        {:reason :origin-not-attached,\n                         :segment (:yin.k/segment marker)})))\n      ;; the arity is that of a `:closure` of the attached code whose body\n      ;; this is, never the wire's\n      (when-not (some #(and (= :closure (nth % 0))\n                            (= (:yin.k/arity marker) (nth % 2))\n                            (= pc (nth % 3)))\n                      (:instructions (:segment vm)))\n        (engine/marker-mismatch! marker))\n      (values/closure\n        (:owner vm)\n        (cond-> {:type :closure,\n                 :arity (:yin.k/arity marker),\n                 :body-pc pc,\n                 :frames (mapv #(mapv decode %) (:yin.k/frames marker))}\n          (:yin.k/store-of marker)\n          (assoc :store-of (:yin.k/store-of marker))))))\n  (gc-roots [vm]\n    {:kernel [(:continuation vm)],\n     :values [(:frames vm) (:registers vm) (:value vm)]})\n  ;; A register payload (a wait, ready or parked entry, or a reified\n  ;; continuation) names the code space as `:segment`; that is code, so\n  ;; every other key is traced. Closures and return frames hold no code.\n  (gc-children [_ x]\n    (when (and (map? x) (= format-tag (:format x)))\n      {:values (into [] (vals (dissoc x :segment)))})))\n","numLines":964,"startLine":1,"totalLines":964}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MeT21B4uxPHXaEAaY6JyHn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
